      "generated_answer": "In the context of network latency analysis with a static congestion window $W$, when the time to transmit a window of data exceeds the round-trip time ($W \\cdot S/R > RTT + S/R$), the link becomes saturated and a queuing delay is introduced. The latency formula for transferring a file of size $O$ (consisting of $k$ segments) in this scenario is derived as $Latency = 2RTT + \\frac{O}{R} + (k-1)[\\frac{W \\cdot S}{R} - (RTT + \\frac{S}{R})]$. This account for the initial handshake, transmission time, and the cumulative delay caused by the window constraint being larger than the RTT.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
