    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read all input from stdin\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    # First value is N\n    n = int(input_data[0])\n    \n    # Store the shoulder heights (A) and head heights (B)\n    # The total head height is the sum of A_i of all giants except the topmost one,\n    # plus the head height B_i of the topmost giant.\n    # To maximize this: Total = (Sum of all A_i) - A_top + B_top\n    # Total = (Sum of all A_i) + (B_top - A_top)\n    # To maximize this, we need to pick the giant with the largest (B_i - A_i) \n    # to be the topmost giant.\n    \n    sum_a = 0\n    max_diff = -1\n    \n    idx = 1\n    for _ in range(n):\n        a = int(input_data[idx])\n        b = int(input_data[idx + 1])\n        sum_a += a\n        \n        diff = b - a\n        if diff > max_diff:\n            max_diff = diff\n            \n        idx += 2\n        \n    print(sum_a + max_diff)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
