    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef findLatestTime(s: str) -> str:\n    s_list = list(s)\n    \n    # Handle Hours HH\n    if s_list[0] == '?' and s_list[1] == '?':\n        s_list[0] = '1'\n        s_list[1] = '1'\n    elif s_list[0] == '?':\n        # If HH is ?X, and X is 0 or 1, we can pick 1 to get 10 or 11.\n        # If X is > 1, we must pick 0 to get 0X.\n        if int(s_list[1]) <= 1:\n            s_list[0] = '1'\n        else:\n            s_list[0] = '0'\n    elif s_list[1] == '?':\n        # If HH is 1?, max is 11. If 0?, max is 09.\n        if s_list[0] == '1':\n            s_list[1] = '1'\n        else:\n            s_list[1] = '9'\n            \n    # Handle Minutes MM\n    if s_list[3] == '?':\n        s_list[3] = '5'\n    if s_list[4] == '?':\n        s_list[4] = '9'\n        \n    return \"\".join(s_list)\n```",
