      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef countSpecialLetters(word: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of special letters in a string.\n    A letter is special if it appears both in lowercase and uppercase.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Use a set to store unique characters for O(1) average lookup\n    chars = set(word)\n    special_count = 0\n    \n    # Iterate through lowercase letters 'a' through 'z'\n    # ord('a') is 97, ord('z') is 122\n    for i in range(26):\n        lower = chr(ord('a') + i)\n        upper = chr(ord('A') + i)\n        \n        # Check if both versions exist in the set\n        if lower in chars and upper in chars:\n            special_count += 1\n            \n    return special_count\n```",
