in all of C_1, C_2, C_3 is (6\\leq x\\leq 7)\\land (6\\leq y\\leq 7) \\land (0\\leq z\\leq 7), with a volume of (7-6)\\times(7-6)\\times(7-0)=7.\n- The region contained in exactly two of C_1, C_2, C_3 is ((0\\leq x < 6)\\land (6\\leq y\\leq 7) \\land (0\\leq z\\leq 7))\\lor((6\\leq x\\leq 7)\\land (0\\leq y < 6) \\land (0\\leq z\\leq 7)), with a volume of (6-0)\\times(7-6)\\times(7-0)\\times 2=84.\n- The region contained in exactly one of C_1, C_2, C_3 has a volume of 840.\n\nThus, all conditions are satisfied.\n(a_1, b_1, c_1, a_2, b_2, c_2, a_3, b_3, c_3) = (-10, 0, 0, -10, 0, 6, -10, 6, 1) also satisfies all conditions and would be a valid output.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n343 34 3\n\nSample Output 2\n\nNo\n\nNo nine integers a_1, b_1, c_1, a_2, b_2, c_2, a_3, b_3, c_3 satisfy all of the conditions.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    V1, V2, V3 = map(int, input_data)\n\n    # We can fix the first cube at (0, 0, 0).\n    # To explore the overlap of three cubes, the relative positions (a2, b2, c2)\n    # and (a3, b3, c3) can range from -7 to 7 because if a coordinate is outside\n    # this range, the intersection volume in that dimension becomes 0.\n    \n    # Precompute intersection length of two intervals [0, 7] and [pos, pos+7]\n    def get_overlap(p1, p2):\n        # Overlap of [p1, p1+7] and [p2, p2+7] is [max(p1, p2), min(p1+7, p2+7)]\n        # Length is max(0, 7 - abs(p1 - p2))\n        return max(0, 7 - abs(p1 - p2))\n\n    # Overlap of [0, 7], [p2, p2+7], [p3, p3+7]\n    def get_overlap3(p1, p2, p3):\n        low = max(p1, p2, p3)\n        high = min(p1 + 7, p2 + 7, p3 + 7)\n        return max(0, high - low)\n\n    # Search space: a2, b2, c2 and a3, b3, c3 in [0, 7] is sufficient for relative overlaps\n    # because shift/sign is symmetric for volumes.\n    for a2 in range(8):\n        for b2 in range(8):\n            for c2 in range(8):\n                # Vol(C1 cap C2)\n                v12 = get_overlap(0, a2) * get_overlap(0, b2) * get_overlap(0, c2)\n                for a3 in range(-7, 8):\n                    for b3 in range(-7, 8):\n                        for c3 in range(-7, 8):\n                            # Vol(C1 cap C3)\n                            v13 = get_overlap(0, a3) * get_overlap(0, b3) * get_overlap(0, c3)\n                            # Vol(C2 cap C3)\n                            v23 = get_overlap(a2, a3) * get_overlap(b2, b3) * get_overlap(c2, c3)\n                            # Vol(C1 cap C2 cap C3)\n                            v123 = get_overlap3(0, a2, a3) * get_overlap3(0, b2, b3) * get_overlap3(0, c2, c3)\n                            \n                            if v123 != V3:\n                                continue\n                            \n                            # Inclusion-Exclusion for volumes:\n                            # Vol(exactly 3) = v123\n                            # Vol(exactly 2) = (v12 - v123) + (v13 - v123) + (v23 - v123)\n                            # Vol(exactly 1) = (7^3 - v12 - v13 + v123) + (7^3 - v12 - v23 + v123) + (7^3 - v13 - v23 + v123)\n                            # Wait, the formula for exactly 1 is simpler:\n                            # Vol(exactly 1) = (Vol(C1) + Vol(C2) + Vol(C3)) - 2*(Vol(exactly 2)) - 3*(Vol(exactly 3))\n                            # Or: Vol(exactly 1) = (3 * 7**3) - 2 * (v12 + v13 + v23 - 3*v123) - 3 * v123\n                            # Simplified:\n                            current_V2 = (v12 + v13 + v23) - 3 * v123\n                            current_V1 = 3 * 343 - 2 * (v12 + v13 + v23) + 3 * v123\n                            \n                            if current_V2 == V2 and current_V1 == V1:\n                                print(\"Yes\")\n                                print(f\"0 0 0 {a2} {b2} {c2} {a3} {b3} {c3}\")\n                                return\n\n    print(\"No\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
