    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read input from stdin\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    N = int(input_data[0])\n    X = int(input_data[1])\n    T = list(map(int, input_data[2:]))\n    \n    MOD = 998244353\n    \n    # dp[t] = probability that a new song starts exactly at time t\n    dp = [0] * (X + 1)\n    \n    # At time 0, a song always starts.\n    dp[0] = 1\n    \n    # Precompute the inverse of N for modulo operations\n    inv_N = pow(N, MOD - 2, MOD)\n    \n    # Calculate DP\n    # dp[t] = sum(dp[t - T_i] * (1/N)) for all i where t - T_i >= 0\n    for t in range(1, X + 1):\n        current_prob = 0\n        for length in T:\n            if t - length >= 0:\n                current_prob = (current_prob + dp[t - length]) % MOD\n        dp[t] = (current_prob * inv_N) % MOD\n    \n    # Song 1 is being played at (X + 0.5) if it started at some time 's'\n    # such that s <= X and s + T[0] > X.\n    # This means the start time 's' must be in the range [max(0, X - T[0] + 1), X].\n    \n    ans = 0\n    T1 = T[0]\n    for s in range(max(0, X - T1 + 1), X + 1):\n        # The probability that a song starts at time 's' is dp[s].\n        # The probability that the *first* song is the one that starts at time 's' is 1/N.\n        # Exception: at time 0, the first song is chosen with 1/N probability as well.\n        # So for all s, the probability is dp[s] * (1/N).\n        ans = (ans + dp[s] * inv_N) % MOD\n        \n    print(ans)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
