      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef sortVowels(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a string s, permutes the vowels such that they are sorted by ASCII values\n    while keeping consonants in their original positions.\n    \"\"\"\n    vowels_set = set(\"aeiouAEIOU\")\n    \n    # Extract all vowels found in the string\n    extracted_vowels = [char for char in s if char in vowels_set]\n    \n    # Sort the extracted vowels based on their ASCII values\n    extracted_vowels.sort()\n    \n    # Reconstruct the string\n    result = []\n    vowel_idx = 0\n    for char in s:\n        if char in vowels_set:\n            # Place the next sorted vowel\n            result.append(extracted_vowels[vowel_idx])\n            vowel_idx += 1\n        else:\n            # Place the original consonant\n            result.append(char)\n            \n    return \"\".join(result)\n```",
