nword consists only of lowercase English letters.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minimumTime(word: str, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the minimum time greater than zero required for word to revert to its \n    initial state by removing k characters from the front and adding any k characters \n    to the end.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(word)\n    # The problem asks for the minimum number of operations (seconds) 't'.\n    # After 't' seconds, we have removed t * k characters from the front.\n    # If t * k >= n, the entire word is replaced, so we can always reconstruct the original word.\n    # If t * k < n, the suffix starting at index t * k must match the prefix of the original word.\n    \n    # Iterate through each second 't'\n    for t in range(1, (n + k - 1) // k + 1):\n        start_index = t * k\n        \n        # If we've removed more or equal characters than the word length, \n        # we can complete the word with any characters (including the original ones).\n        if start_index >= n:\n            return t\n        \n        # Check if the remaining suffix of the word matches the beginning of the original word.\n        # word[start_index:] is what remains of the original string.\n        # word[:n-start_index] is the prefix it needs to match.\n        if word[start_index:] == word[:n - start_index]:\n            return t\n            \n    return (n + k - 1) // k\n```",
