      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef maximumLengthSubstring(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum length of a substring such that it contains \n    at most two occurrences of each character using a sliding window approach.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_len = 0\n    left = 0\n    counts = {}\n    \n    for right in range(len(s)):\n        char_right = s[right]\n        counts[char_right] = counts.get(char_right, 0) + 1\n        \n        # If the current character count exceeds 2, shrink the window from the left\n        while counts[char_right] > 2:\n            char_left = s[left]\n            counts[char_left] -= 1\n            left += 1\n            \n        # Update the maximum length found so far\n        max_len = max(max_len, right - left + 1)\n        \n    return max_len\n```",
