      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read the input string from stdin and strip any surrounding whitespace\n    s = sys.stdin.read().strip()\n    \n    if not s:\n        return\n\n    # Dictionary to store the frequency of each character\n    counts = {}\n    for char in s:\n        counts[char] = counts.get(char, 0) + 1\n    \n    # Find the maximum frequency value\n    max_freq = max(counts.values())\n    \n    # Identify all characters that have the maximum frequency\n    most_frequent_chars = [char for char, count in counts.items() if count == max_freq]\n    \n    # Sort them alphabetically and pick the first one\n    result = sorted(most_frequent_chars)[0]\n    \n    # Print the result\n    print(result)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
