      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef furthestDistanceFromOrigin(moves: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the furthest distance from the origin after n moves.\n    'L' moves left, 'R' moves right, and '_' can be either 'L' or 'R'.\n    To maximize distance, all '_' should be assigned to the direction\n    that already has more moves or is the primary direction.\n    \"\"\"\n    l_count = moves.count('L')\n    r_count = moves.count('R')\n    underscore_count = moves.count('_')\n    \n    # The maximum distance is the absolute difference between L and R,\n    # plus the count of underscores (which can all be assigned to the\n    # dominant direction to maximize displacement).\n    return abs(l_count - r_count) + underscore_count\n```",
