    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read all input from standard input\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    # N: number of people, D: max infection distance\n    N = int(input_data[0])\n    D = int(input_data[1])\n    \n    # Square of D to avoid using sqrt in distance calculations\n    D_squared = D * D\n    \n    # Store coordinates of each person\n    coords = []\n    ptr = 2\n    for _ in range(N):\n        x = int(input_data[ptr])\n        y = int(input_data[ptr+1])\n        coords.append((x, y))\n        ptr += 2\n        \n    # infected[i] tracks if person i is infected\n    infected = [False] * N\n    # Person 1 (index 0) is initially infected\n    infected[0] = True\n    \n    # Use a stack (DFS) or queue (BFS) to spread the virus\n    # Starting with person 1 (index 0)\n    stack = [0]\n    \n    while stack:\n        current_idx = stack.pop()\n        curr_x, curr_y = coords[current_idx]\n        \n        for i in range(N):\n            if not infected[i]:\n                target_x, target_y = coords[i]\n                # Calculate squared Euclidean distance\n                dist_sq = (curr_x - target_x)**2 + (curr_y - target_y)**2\n                \n                if dist_sq <= D_squared:\n                    infected[i] = True\n                    stack.append(i)\n    \n    # Output the result for each person\n    results = []\n    for i in range(N):\n        if infected[i]:\n            results.append(\"Yes\")\n        else:\n            results.append(\"No\")\n    \n    sys.stdout.write(\"\\n\".join(results) + \"\\n\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
