    "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. Return the function body without invoking it at the final solution. Question:\nYou are given an array arr of size n consisting of non-empty strings.\nFind a string array answer of size n such that:\n\nanswer[i] is the shortest substring of arr[i] that does not occur as a substring in any other string in arr. If multiple such substrings exist, answer[i] should be the lexicographically smallest. And if no such substring exists, answer[i] should be an empty string.\n\nReturn the array answer.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: arr = [\"cab\",\"ad\",\"bad\",\"c\"]\nOutput: [\"ab\",\"\",\"ba\",\"\"]\nExplanation: We have the following:\n- For the string \"cab\", the shortest substring that does not occur in any other string is either \"ca\" or \"ab\", we choose the lexicographically smaller substring, which is \"ab\".\n- For the string \"ad\", there is no substring that does not occur in any other string.\n- For the string \"bad\", the shortest substring that does not occur in any other string is \"ba\".\n- For the string \"c\", there is no substring that does not occur in any other string.\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: arr = [\"abc\",\"bcd\",\"abcd\"]\nOutput: [\"\",\"\",\"abcd\"]\nExplanation: We have the following:\n- For the string \"abc\", there is no substring that does not occur in any other string.\n- For the string \"bcd\", there is no substring that does not occur in any other string.\n- For the string \"abcd\", the shortest substring that does not occur in any other string is \"abcd\".\n\n \nConstraints:\n\nn == arr.length\n2 <= n <= 100\n1 <= arr[i].length <= 20\narr[i] consists only of lowercase English letters.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef shortestSubstrings(arr):\n    n = len(arr)\n    # Precompute a list of maps/counters to store occurrences of all substrings\n    # across the entire array.\n    from collections import Counter\n    \n    # Global count of how many strings in arr contain each specific substring\n    substring_counts = Counter()\n    \n    # To count correctly, we must only count a substring once per index i\n    for s in arr:\n        unique_subs_in_s = set()\n        m = len(s)\n        for length in range(1, m + 1):\n            for i in range(m - length + 1):\n                unique_subs_in_s.add(s[i:i+length])\n        for sub in unique_subs_in_s:\n            substring_counts[sub] += 1\n            \n    answer = []\n    for s in arr:\n        m = len(s)\n        best_sub = \"\"\n        \n        # Check substrings by length first to satisfy \"shortest\" constraint\n        found_for_length = False\n        for length in range(1, m + 1):\n            candidates = []\n            for i in range(m - length + 1):\n                sub = s[i:i+length]\n                # A substring is unique to this string if it appears in exactly 1 string in arr\n                if substring_counts[sub] == 1:\n                    candidates.append(sub)\n            \n            if candidates:\n                # If we found unique substrings of this length,\n                # pick the lexicographically smallest one.\n                candidates.sort()\n                best_sub = candidates[0]\n                found_for_length = True\n                break\n        \n        answer.append(best_sub)\n        \n    return answer\n```",
