      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minimizeConcatenatedLength(words):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum possible length of the string formed by joining words \n    in the given order, choosing to append or prepend each new word.\n    \n    The state is defined by dp[i][first_char][last_char], representing the \n    minimum length after processing i words, where the resulting string \n    starts with first_char and ends with last_char.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(words)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    \n    # dp[first_char][last_char] stores the minimum length for the current string\n    # Characters are mapped to 0-25\n    dp = {}\n    \n    # Initial state: the first word\n    first_word = words[0]\n    start_char = ord(first_word[0]) - ord('a')\n    end_char = ord(first_word[-1]) - ord('a')\n    dp[(start_char, end_char)] = len(first_word)\n    \n    for i in range(1, n):\n        word = words[i]\n        w_len = len(word)\n        w_start = ord(word[0]) - ord('a')\n        w_end = ord(word[-1]) - ord('a')\n        \n        next_dp = {}\n        \n        for (head, tail), length in dp.items():\n            # Option 1: Join current word to the end (str = join(str_prev, word))\n            # if tail == w_start, we save 1 character\n            cost_append = length + w_len - (1 if tail == w_start else 0)\n            state_append = (head, w_end)\n            if state_append not in next_dp or cost_append < next_dp[state_append]:\n                next_dp[state_append] = cost_append\n                \n            # Option 2: Join current word to the front (str = join(word, str_prev))\n            # if w_end == head, we save 1 character\n            cost_prepend = length + w_len - (1 if w_end == head else 0)\n            state_prepend = (w_start, tail)\n            if state_prepend not in next_dp or cost_prepend < next_dp[state_prepend]:\n                next_dp[state_prepend] = cost_prepend\n        \n        dp = next_dp\n        \n    return min(dp.value