    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef check_airport_code():\n    # Read S and T from standard input\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    s = input_data[0]\n    t = input_data[1]\n    \n    # Target characters to find in S (lowercase version of T)\n    t_lower = t.lower()\n    \n    # Greedily match characters of T in S to find the longest possible subsequence\n    # that matches the prefix of T.\n    match_count = 0\n    s_idx = 0\n    \n    # We only need to check at most the first 3 characters of T\n    # (or the first 2 if we are considering the 'X' suffix rule)\n    target_len = 3\n    \n    for char in t_lower:\n        # Try to find the current character of T in S starting from current s_idx\n        found = False\n        while s_idx < len(s):\n            if s[s_idx] == char:\n                match_count += 1\n                s_idx += 1\n                found = True\n                break\n            s_idx += 1\n        \n        # If we can't find the current character, we can't match any more of T\n        if not found:\n            break\n            \n    # Method 1: Subsequence of length 3\n    if match_count == 3:\n        print(\"Yes\")\n        return\n    \n    # Method 2: Subsequence of length 2 and the last char of T is 'X'\n    if match_count == 2 and t[2] == 'X':\n        print(\"Yes\")\n        return\n        \n    print(\"No\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    check_airport_code()\n```",
