      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read all input data\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    ptr = 0\n    \n    # N: Number of people\n    N = int(input_data[ptr])\n    ptr += 1\n    \n    # P: The order of people (person at i-th position)\n    # We store the position of each person in a dictionary or array for O(1) lookup\n    # pos[person_id] = position (index in line)\n    pos = {}\n    for i in range(N):\n        person_id = int(input_data[ptr])\n        pos[person_id] = i\n        ptr += 1\n        \n    # Q: Number of queries\n    Q = int(input_data[ptr])\n    ptr += 1\n    \n    # Process each query\n    results = []\n    for _ in range(Q):\n        A = int(input_data[ptr])\n        B = int(input_data[ptr+1])\n        ptr += 2\n        \n        # Compare positions. Smaller position index means further to the front.\n        if pos[A] < pos[B]:\n            results.append(str(A))\n        else:\n            results.append(str(B))\n            \n    # Print all results separated by newlines\n    sys.stdout.write(\"\\n\".join(results) + \"\\n\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
