      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minChanges(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    To make a binary string beautiful, it must be partitionable into even-length \n    substrings of identical characters. Since the minimum even length is 2, \n    the most efficient way to satisfy the condition is to ensure that every \n    disjoint pair (s[0]s[1], s[2]s[3], ..., s[n-2]s[n-1]) consists of the \n    same character. If a pair has different characters (e.g., \"01\" or \"10\"), \n    one change is required to make them identical (\"00\" or \"11\").\n    \"\"\"\n    changes = 0\n    # Iterate through the string in steps of 2\n    for i in range(0, len(s), 2):\n        # If the characters in the current pair are different, we need one change\n        if s[i] != s[i + 1]:\n            changes += 1\n    return changes\n```",
