    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read all input from stdin\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    t = int(input_data[0])\n    ptr = 1\n    \n    results = []\n    for _ in range(t):\n        n = int(input_data[ptr])\n        ptr += 1\n        a = []\n        for i in range(n):\n            a.append(int(input_data[ptr]))\n            ptr += 1\n        \n        # To maximize the product by adding 1 to exactly one element,\n        # it is always optimal to add 1 to the smallest element in the array.\n        # This is because (x+1)*y = xy + y. To maximize this, we need the \n        # remaining product y (product of all other numbers) to be as large \n        # as possible, which happens when the incremented number x is the smallest.\n        \n        a.sort()\n        a[0] += 1\n        \n        product = 1\n        for num in a:\n            product *= num\n        results.append(str(product))\n    \n    # Print all results separated by newlines\n    sys.stdout.write(\"\\n\".join(results) + \"\\n\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
