    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\n# Increase recursion depth for deep trees\nsys.setrecursionlimit(10**6)\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read N from standard input\n    line = sys.stdin.readline()\n    if not line:\n        return\n    n = int(line.strip())\n    \n    # Adjacency list to represent the tree\n    adj = [[] for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    for _ in range(n - 1):\n        try:\n            u, v = map(int, sys.stdin.readline().split())\n            adj[u].append(v)\n            adj[v].append(u)\n        except ValueError:\n            break\n\n    # If vertex 1 is already a leaf (degree <= 1), \n    # it can be removed in the first operation.\n    if len(adj[1]) <= 1:\n        print(1)\n        return\n\n    # dp[u] stores the number of operations needed to remove the subtree rooted at u\n    # (where u is considered a leaf relative to its parent).\n    # To remove vertex 1, we need to remove all but one of its subtrees\n    # so that vertex 1 becomes a leaf.\n    \n    memo = {}\n\n    def get_subtree_size(u, p):\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculates the number of nodes in the subtree rooted at u.\n        To make u a leaf relative to its parent, we must delete all nodes \n        in its subtrees.\n        \"\"\"\n        count = 1\n        for v in adj[u]:\n            if v != p:\n                count += get_subtree_size(v, u)\n        return count\n\n    # To delete vertex 1, it must become a leaf.\n    # Vertex 1 is a leaf if it has only one neighbor.\n    # We should keep the neighbor that has the largest subtree attached to it\n    # and delete all other neighbors' subtrees to minimize operations.\n    \n    subtree_costs = []\n    for neighbor in adj[1]:\n        # Cost to remove the branch starting at 'neighbor'\n        subtree_costs.append(get_subtree_size(neighbor, 1))\n    \n    # Total operations = (sum of costs of branches to remove) + 1 (for vertex 1 itself)\n    # To minimize this, we exclude the branch with the maximum cost.\n    total_nodes_in_branches = sum(subtree_costs)\n    max_branch_size = max(subtree_costs)\n    \n    ans = (total_nodes_in_branches - max_branch_size) + 1\n    print(ans)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
