    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef longestSemiRepetitiveSubstring(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the length of the longest semi-repetitive substring inside s.\n    A semi-repetitive string has at most one consecutive pair of the same digits.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    if n <= 1:\n        return n\n    \n    max_len = 0\n    left = 0\n    last_pair_index = -1  # Stores the index of the second digit in the last found pair\n    \n    # We use a sliding window [left, right]\n    for right in range(1, n):\n        # Check if we found a consecutive pair\n        if s[right] == s[right - 1]:\n            # If we already had a pair in the current window, \n            # move the left pointer to the position after the first pair's start\n            if last_pair_index != -1:\n                left = last_pair_index\n            \n            # Update the most recent pair's position\n            last_pair_index = right\n            \n        # Calculate window length: right - left + 1\n        max_len = max(max_len, right - left + 1)\n        \n    # If no pairs were found, max_len would still be 0 (for n > 1), so handle base case\n    return max(max_len, 1)\n```",
