    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef minimumDeletions(word: str, k: int) -> int:\n    # Count the frequency of each character in the word\n    counts = Counter(word)\n    # Get the sorted list of frequencies\n    freqs = sorted(counts.values())\n    \n    n = len(freqs)\n    min_deletions = float('inf')\n    \n    # Prefix sum to quickly calculate deletions for frequencies smaller than a target\n    prefix_sum = [0] * (n + 1)\n    for i in range(n):\n        prefix_sum[i + 1] = prefix_sum[i] + freqs[i]\n    \n    # Iterate through each unique frequency in the word and treat it as the \n    # potential minimum frequency (target_min) for a k-special string.\n    for i in range(n):\n        target_min = freqs[i]\n        target_max = target_min + k\n        \n        # 1. Deletions needed for all characters with frequency less than target_min:\n        # These characters must be removed entirely.\n        deletions_below = prefix_sum[i]\n        \n        # 2. Deletions needed for all characters with frequency greater than target_max:\n        # These characters must be reduced to target_max.\n        deletions_above = 0\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            if freqs[j] > target_max:\n                deletions_above += (freqs[j] - target_max)\n        \n        total_deletions = deletions_below + deletions_above\n        min_deletions = min(min_deletions, total_deletions)\n        \n    return min_deletions\n```",
