      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef sumCounts(nums):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the squares of distinct counts of all subarrays of nums.\n    \n    Constraints:\n    1 <= nums.length <= 100\n    1 <= nums[i] <= 100\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(nums)\n    total_sum = 0\n    \n    # Iterate through all possible starting indices of a subarray\n    for i in range(n):\n        # Use a set to track distinct elements for subarrays starting at index i\n        distinct_elements = set()\n        # Iterate through all possible ending indices for the subarray starting at i\n        for j in range(i, n):\n            distinct_elements.add(nums[j])\n            # The size of the set is the distinct count\n            count = len(distinct_elements)\n            # Add the square of the distinct count to the total sum\n            total_sum += count ** 2\n            \n    return total_sum\n```",
