      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read the input H from standard input\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    H = int(input_data[0])\n    \n    # Initial setup\n    # Day 0: Height is 0.\n    # On night 0, height increases by 2^0 = 1.\n    # Morning of Day 1: Height is 1.\n    # Morning of Day n: Height is 2^0 + 2^1 + ... + 2^(n-1) = 2^n - 1.\n    \n    # We need to find the smallest n such that (2^n - 1) > H.\n    # This is equivalent to 2^n > H + 1.\n    \n    day = 0\n    plant_height = 0\n    \n    while plant_height <= H:\n        # The height increase happens at the night of the previous day.\n        # The morning of 'day + 1' will see the result of the growth on night 'day'.\n        plant_height += 2**day\n        day += 1\n        \n    print(day)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
