    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef approximate_n():\n    # Read input from stdin\n    line = sys.stdin.readline()\n    if not line:\n        return\n    \n    n_str = line.strip()\n    if not n_str:\n        return\n    \n    n = int(n_str)\n    \n    # Apply approximation rules based on the range of N\n    if n <= 10**3 - 1:\n        # If N is less than or equal to 10^3-1, print N as it is.\n        print(n)\n    elif 10**3 <= n <= 10**4 - 1:\n        # Truncate the ones digit\n        print((n // 10) * 10)\n    elif 10**4 <= n <= 10**5 - 1:\n        # Truncate the tens digit and below\n        print((n // 100) * 100)\n    elif 10**5 <= n <= 10**6 - 1:\n        # Truncate the hundreds digit and below\n        print((n // 1000) * 1000)\n    elif 10**6 <= n <= 10**7 - 1:\n        # Truncate the thousands digit and below\n        print((n // 10000) * 10000)\n    elif 10**7 <= n <= 10**8 - 1:\n        # Truncate the ten-thousands digit and below\n        print((n // 100000) * 100000)\n    elif 10**8 <= n <= 10**9 - 1:\n        # Truncate the hundred-thousands digit and below\n        print((n // 1000000) * 1000000)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    approximate_n()\n```",
