      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef buyChoco(prices, money):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the leftover money after buying exactly two chocolates such that the\n    sum of their prices is minimized and non-negative leftover money remains.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Sort the prices to find the two cheapest chocolates\n    prices.sort()\n    \n    # The sum of the two cheapest chocolates\n    min_cost = prices[0] + prices[1]\n    \n    # If we can afford the two cheapest chocolates, return the leftover\n    if min_cost <= money:\n        return money - min_cost\n    \n    # Otherwise, return the original amount of money\n    return money\n```",
