    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read all input from stdin\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    N = int(input_data[0])\n    \n    # Initialize the distance matrix\n    # dist[i][j] will store the weight of the edge between vertex i and j\n    dist = [[0] * N for _ in range(N)]\n    \n    curr = 1\n    for i in range(N - 1):\n        for j in range(i + 1, N):\n            weight = int(input_data[curr])\n            dist[i][j] = weight\n            dist[j][i] = weight\n            curr += 1\n            \n    # dp[mask] stores the maximum total weight for the set of vertices represented by 'mask'\n    # Mask is a bitmask where the i-th bit is 1 if vertex i is used.\n    dp = [0] * (1 << N)\n    \n    # Iterate through all possible subsets of vertices\n    for mask in range(1 << N):\n        # Find the first vertex 'i' that is NOT in the current mask\n        i = -1\n        for bit in range(N):\n            if not (mask & (1 << bit)):\n                i = bit\n                break\n        \n        # If all vertices are used, skip\n        if i == -1:\n            continue\n            \n        # Option 1: Leave vertex 'i' unused and transition to the next state\n        next_mask_without_i = mask | (1 << i)\n        if dp[next_mask_without_i] < dp[mask]:\n            dp[next_mask_without_i] = dp[mask]\n            \n        # Option 2: Pair vertex 'i' with another unused vertex 'j'\n        for j in range(i + 1, N):\n            if not (mask & (1 << j)):\n                next_mask_with_pair = mask | (1 << i) | (1 << j)\n                new_weight = dp[mask] + dist[i][j]\n                if dp[next_mask_with_pair] < new_weight:\n                    dp[next_mask_with_pair] = new_weight\n                    \n    # The answer is the maximum value in the dp table\n    print(max(dp))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
