      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read H and W\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    H = int(input_data[0])\n    W = int(input_data[1])\n    S = input_data[2:]\n\n    # Find the boundaries of the original rectangle\n    # The rectangle must contain at least one cookie now.\n    min_r, max_r = H, -1\n    min_c, max_c = W, -1\n\n    for r in range(H):\n        for c in range(W):\n            if S[r][c] == '#':\n                if r < min_r: min_r = r\n                if r > max_r: max_r = r\n                if c < min_c: min_c = c\n                if c > max_c: max_c = c\n\n    # The original rectangle was bounded by min_r, max_r, min_c, max_c.\n    # We iterate through this range to find the single '.' which is the missing cookie.\n    for r in range(min_r, max_r + 1):\n        for c in range(min_c, max_c + 1):\n            if S[r][c] == '.':\n                # Rows and columns are 1-indexed in output\n                print(f\"{r + 1} {c + 1}\")\n                return\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
