      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef relocateMarbles(nums, moveFrom, moveTo):\n    \"\"\"\n    Relocates marbles based on the provided moves and returns the sorted unique occupied positions.\n    \n    Since the problem states that all marbles at moveFrom[i] are moved to moveTo[i],\n    we only need to track the set of unique positions occupied by marbles.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Use a set to keep track of unique occupied positions\n    occupied_positions = set(nums)\n    \n    # Iterate through the move steps\n    for f, t in zip(moveFrom, moveTo):\n        # Remove the old position if it exists in the set\n        # (The problem guarantees a marble is present at moveFrom[i])\n        occupied_positions.discard(f)\n        # Add the new position to the set\n        occupied_positions.add(t)\n    \n    # Return the occupied positions sorted in ascending order\n    return sorted(list(occupied_positions))\n```",
