    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef longestCommonPrefix(arr1, arr2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the length of the longest common prefix among all pairs (x, y)\n    where x is from arr1 and y is from arr2.\n    \"\"\"\n    prefixes = set()\n    \n    # Store all possible prefixes of every number in arr1 in a hash set\n    for val in arr1:\n        s = str(val)\n        # Generate all prefixes for the current number\n        # e.g., for 123, prefixes are \"1\", \"12\", \"123\"\n        for i in range(1, len(s) + 1):\n            prefixes.add(s[:i])\n            \n    max_len = 0\n    \n    # Check all possible prefixes of every number in arr2\n    for val in arr2:\n        s = str(val)\n        # Check from the longest possible prefix to the shortest\n        # Optimization: start checking from the current max_len + 1\n        for i in range(len(s), max_len, -1):\n            if s[:i] in prefixes:\n                max_len = max(max_len, i)\n                break # Found the longest prefix for this specific val in arr2\n                \n    return max_len\n```",
