    "global index": "LiveCodeBench_420",
    "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. The function should take stdin as input and print the output. Simply call the function after the definition. Question:\nYou are given a tree with N vertices. The vertices are numbered 1 to N, and the i-th edge connects vertices A_i and B_i.\nYou are also given a sequence of positive integers C = (C_1, C_2, \\ldots ,C_N) of length N. Let d(a, b) be the number of edges between vertices a and b, and for x = 1, 2, \\ldots, N, let \\displaystyle f(x) = \\sum_{{i=1}}^{{N}} (C_i \\times d(x, i)). Find \\displaystyle \\min_{{1 \\leq v \\leq N}} f(v).\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nN\nA_1 B_1\nA_2 B_2\n\\vdots\nA_{{N - 1}} B_{{N - 1}}\nC_1 C_2 \\cdots C_N\n\nOutput\n\nPrint the answer in one line.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- 1 \\leq N \\leq 10^5\n- 1 \\leq A_i, B_i \\leq N\n- The given graph is a tree.\n- 1 \\leq C_i \\leq 10^9\n\nSample Input 1\n\n4\n1 2\n1 3\n2 4\n1 1 1 2\n\nSample Output 1\n\n5\n\nFor example, consider calculating f(1). We have d(1, 1) = 0, d(1, 2) = 1, d(1, 3) = 1, d(1, 4) = 2.\nThus, f(1) = 0 \\times 1 + 1 \\times 1 + 1 \\times 1 + 2 \\times 2 = 6.\nSimilarly, f(2) = 5, f(3) = 9, f(4) = 6. Since f(2) is the minimum, print 5.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n2\n2 1\n1 1000000000\n\nSample Output 2\n\n1\n\nf(2) = 1, which is the minimum.\n\nSample Input 3\n\n7\n7 3\n2 5\n2 4\n3 1\n3 6\n2 1\n2 7 6 9 3 4 6\n\nSample Output 3\n\n56",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\n# Increase recursion depth for deep trees\nsys.setrecursionlimit(200000)\n\ndef solve():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    N = int(input_data[0])\n    if N == 1:\n        print(0)\n        return\n        \n    adj = [[] for _ in range(N + 1)]\n    idx = 1\n    for _ in range(N - 1):\n        u = int(input_data[idx])\n        v = int(input_data[idx + 1])\n        adj[u].append(v)\n        adj[v].append(u)\n        idx += 2\n        \n    C = [0] * (N + 1)\n    for i in range(1, N + 1):\n        C[i] = int(input_data[idx])\n        idx += 1\n        \n    # sum_c[u] stores the sum of C_i in the subtree rooted at u\n    sum_c = [0] * (N + 1)\n    # f[1] will be calculated manually, then used to derive others\n    total_c = sum(C)\n    \n    # We'll use a standard rerooting DP approach.\n    # First pass: calculate sum_c and initial f(1)\n    # Using iterative DFS to avoid recursion depth issues in some environments\n    parent = [0] * (N + 1)\n    order = []\n    stack = [1]\n    visited = [False] * (N + 1)\n    visited[1] = True\n    \n    while stack:\n        u = stack.pop()\n        order.append(u)\n        for v in adj[u]:\n            if not visited[v]:\n                visited[v] = True\n                parent[v] = u\n                stack.append(v)\n                \n    f1 = 0\n    depth = [0] * (N + 1)\n    # Calculate subtree sums and root value f(1)\n    for u in reversed(order):\n        sum_c[u] += C[u]\n        if parent[u] != 0:\n            sum_c[parent[u]] += sum_c[u]\n            \n    # Calculate distance from root (node 1)\n    for u in order:\n        if parent[u] != 0:\n            depth[u] = depth[parent[u]] + 1\n        f1 += C[u] * depth[u]\n        \n    # Second pass: Rerooting to find all f(x)\n    # f(v) = f(u) - sum_c[v] + (total_c - sum_c[v])\n    # where v is a child of u\n    results = [0] * (N + 1)\n    results[1] = f1\n    for u in order:\n        for v in adj[u]:\n            if v == parent[u]:\n                continue\n            results[v] = results[u] - sum_c[v] + (total_c - sum_c[v])\n            \n    print(min(results[1:]))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n\n```",
