      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read all input at once for performance\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    n = int(input_data[0])\n    \n    # Dictionary to store the minimum deliciousness found for each color\n    # Key: color (C_i), Value: minimum deliciousness (A_i) seen so far for that color\n    min_deliciousness_per_color = {}\n    \n    for i in range(n):\n        a = int(input_data[2 * i + 1])\n        c = int(input_data[2 * i + 2])\n        \n        if c in min_deliciousness_per_color:\n            # If color exists, update the minimum deliciousness for this color\n            if a < min_deliciousness_per_color[c]:\n                min_deliciousness_per_color[c] = a\n        else:\n            # First time seeing this color, initialize with current deliciousness\n            min_deliciousness_per_color[c] = a\n            \n    # We want to choose the color that has the maximum value among these minimums\n    ans = max(min_deliciousness_per_color.values())\n    print(ans)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
