rs' scores at 2.5 seconds from now.\n- After three seconds, the score of player 2 increases by 10 points, making S=\\lbrace 10,10,20\\rbrace. Therefore, there are two different score values among the players' scores at 3.5 seconds from now.\n- After four seconds, the score of player 2 increases by 10 points, making S=\\lbrace 10,20,20\\rbrace. Therefore, there are two different score values among the players' scores at 4.5 seconds from now.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n1 3\n1 3\n1 4\n1 3\n\nSample Output 2\n\n1\n1\n1\n\nSample Input 3\n\n10 10\n7 2620\n9 2620\n8 3375\n1 3375\n6 1395\n5 1395\n6 2923\n10 3375\n9 5929\n5 1225\n\nSample Output 3\n\n2\n2\n3\n3\n4\n4\n5\n5\n6\n5",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Use fast I/O to handle large inputs\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    N = int(input_data[0])\n    T = int(input_data[1])\n    \n    # current_scores[i] stores the current score of player i\n    # Players are 1-indexed, so we use size N+1\n    current_scores = [0] * (N + 1)\n    \n    # score_counts tracks how many players have a specific score\n    # score_counts[score] = count\n    score_counts = {0: N}\n    \n    # distinct_values_count represents the number of unique scores currently present\n    distinct_values_count = 1\n    \n    ptr = 2\n    results = []\n    \n    for _ in range(T):\n        A_i = int(input_data[ptr])\n        B_i = int(input_data[ptr + 1])\n        ptr += 2\n        \n        old_score = current_scores[A_i]\n        new_score = old_score + B_i\n        \n        # Update current score for player A_i\n        current_scores[A_i] = new_score\n        \n        # Update the count for the old score\n        score_counts[old_score] -= 1\n        if score_counts[old_score] == 0:\n            # If no player has this score anymore, decrement distinct count\n            distinct_values_count -= 1\n            # Optional: del score_counts[old_score] to save memory\n        \n        # Update the count for the new score\n        if new_score in score_counts and score_counts[new_score] > 0:\n            score_counts[new_score] += 1\n        else:\n            # If this is a brand new unique score, increment distinct count\n            score_counts[new_score] = 1\n            distinct_values_count += 1\n            \n        results.append(str(distinct_values_count))\n    \n    # Print all results separated by newlines\n    sys.stdout.write(\"\\n\".join(results) + \"\\n\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
