      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef findPeaks(mountain):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds all the peaks in the mountain array.\n    A peak is an element strictly greater than its neighboring elements.\n    First and last elements are excluded.\n    \"\"\"\n    peaks = []\n    # Iterate from index 1 to the second to last index\n    for i in range(1, len(mountain) - 1):\n        # Check if the current element is strictly greater than neighbors\n        if mountain[i] > mountain[i - 1] and mountain[i] > mountain[i + 1]:\n            peaks.append(i)\n    return peaks\n```",
