      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Set recursion limit for deep dependency trees\n    sys.setrecursionlimit(300000)\n    \n    # Read all input at once for performance\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    N = int(input_data[0])\n    \n    # adj[i] will store the list of books required to read book i+1\n    adj = []\n    ptr = 1\n    for i in range(N):\n        c_i = int(input_data[ptr])\n        ptr += 1\n        # Subtract 1 for 0-indexed logic\n        dependencies = [int(x) - 1 for x in input_data[ptr : ptr + c_i]]\n        adj.append(dependencies)\n        ptr += c_i\n        \n    visited = [False] * N\n    result = []\n    \n    def dfs(u):\n        \"\"\"\n        Standard Post-order DFS traversal to find all dependencies.\n        This naturally handles the 'read before' requirement by appending \n        to the result list after visiting all children.\n        \"\"\"\n        visited[u] = True\n        for v in adj[u]:\n            if not visited[v]:\n                dfs(v)\n        # We don't want to include book 1 (index 0) in the output list\n        if u != 0:\n            result.append(u + 1)\n            \n    # Start DFS from book 1\n    dfs(0)\n    \n    # Print the result list separated by spaces\n    if result:\n        print(*(result))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
