      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read the input from stdin\n    line = sys.stdin.readline()\n    if not line:\n        return\n    \n    n = int(line.strip())\n    \n    # The water stations are at points: 0, 5, 10, ..., 100\n    # We are looking for a multiple of 5 that is closest to N.\n    # We can find this by dividing N by 5 and rounding to the nearest integer.\n    \n    # Calculate the remainder when dividing by 5\n    remainder = n % 5\n    \n    if remainder <= 2:\n        # If the remainder is 0, 1, or 2, the nearest station is (n - remainder)\n        print(n - remainder)\n    else:\n        # If the remainder is 3 or 4, the nearest station is (n + (5 - remainder))\n        print(n + (5 - remainder))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
