    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read input from stdin\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    N = int(input_data[0])\n    X = int(input_data[1])\n    A = [int(x) for x in input_data[2:]]\n    \n    # We need to find the minimum score s (0 <= s <= 100) \n    # such that the sum of the middle N-2 elements of (A + [s]) is >= X.\n    \n    ans = -1\n    for s in range(101):\n        # Create the full list of N scores\n        current_scores = A + [s]\n        current_scores.sort()\n        \n        # Calculate the sum of the N-2 scores excluding min and max\n        # S_2 + S_3 + ... + S_{N-1}\n        # In a list of N elements (0 to N-1), this is sum(current_scores[1:N-1])\n        final_grade = sum(current_scores[1:N-1])\n        \n        if final_grade >= X:\n            ans = s\n            break\n            \n    print(ans)\n\n# Execute the function\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
