      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef occurrencesOfElement(nums, queries, x):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the k-th occurrence of x for each query k in queries.\n    \n    Args:\n    nums: List[int] - The input array of integers.\n    queries: List[int] - The list of occurrence ranks to find.\n    x: int - The target integer to find occurrences of.\n    \n    Returns:\n    List[int] - The indices of the occurrences or -1 if the rank exceeds the count.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Pre-process: find all indices where nums[i] == x\n    indices = [i for i, val in enumerate(nums) if val == x]\n    \n    ans = []\n    num_occurrences = len(indices)\n    \n    for q in queries:\n        # Since queries[i] is 1-indexed (1st, 2nd, etc.), \n        # check if it's within the range of our indices list.\n        if q <= num_occurrences:\n            ans.append(indices[q - 1])\n        else:\n            ans.append(-1)\n            \n    return ans\n```",
