      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minimumCost(nums: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    To divide an array into 3 disjoint contiguous subarrays, we always include \n    the first element of the original array (nums[0]) as the cost of the first subarray.\n    We then need to pick two other indices i and j (where 1 <= i < j < n) to be \n    the start of the second and third subarrays. \n    To minimize the total cost, we simply need to find the two smallest values \n    in the remainder of the array (nums[1:]).\n    \"\"\"\n    first_cost = nums[0]\n    # Get all elements from index 1 onwards\n    remaining_elements = nums[1:]\n    # Sort them to find the two smallest values\n    remaining_elements.sort()\n    \n    # The minimum cost is the first element plus the two smallest remaining elements\n    return first_cost + remaining_elements[0] + remaining_elements[1]\n```",
