      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef findMissingAndRepeatedValues(grid):\n    n = len(grid)\n    size = n * n\n    count = {}\n    \n    # Initialize count dictionary for all numbers from 1 to n^2\n    for i in range(1, size + 1):\n        count[i] = 0\n        \n    # Traverse the grid and count occurrences of each number\n    for row in grid:\n        for val in row:\n            count[val] += 1\n            \n    a = -1\n    b = -1\n    \n    # Identify the repeating number (a) and the missing number (b)\n    for num, freq in count.items():\n        if freq == 2:\n            a = num\n        elif freq == 0:\n            b = num\n            \n    return [a, b]\n```",
