      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef getGoodIndices(variables, target):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns an array consisting of indices i where ((a_i^b_i % 10)^c_i) % m_i == target.\n    \n    Args:\n    variables: A 2D list where each element is [a_i, b_i, c_i, m_i].\n    target: An integer to compare the result of the formula against.\n    \n    Returns:\n    A list of good indices.\n    \"\"\"\n    good_indices = []\n    \n    for i, (a, b, c, m) in enumerate(variables):\n        # We use pow(base, exp, mod) for efficient modular exponentiation.\n        # First step: (a^b % 10)\n        first_step = pow(a, b, 10)\n        \n        # Second step: (first_step^c % m)\n        second_step = pow(first_step, c, m)\n        \n        if second_step == target:\n            good_indices.append(i)\n            \n    return good_indices\n```",
