    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read input from stdin\n    line = sys.stdin.readline()\n    if not line:\n        return\n    n = int(line.strip())\n\n    # The maximum value of N is 10^18.\n    # We are looking for x such that x^3 <= N.\n    # x_max = (10^18)^(1/3) = 1,000,000.\n    # We can iterate from x = 1,000,000 down to 1.\n    \n    # Pre-calculating the limit for x\n    # Using integer power to avoid floating point precision issues\n    limit = 10**6 + 1\n    \n    ans = 1\n    # Iterate through all possible integers whose cube could be <= N\n    # We can go from 1 up to 1,000,000 and keep track of the largest valid one\n    for x in range(1, limit + 1):\n        cube = x * x * x\n        if cube > n:\n            break\n        \n        # Check if the cube is a palindrome\n        s = str(cube)\n        if s == s[::-1]:\n            ans = cube\n            \n    print(ans)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
