      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef countAlternatingSubarrays(nums):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the total number of alternating subarrays in a binary array.\n    An alternating subarray is one where no two adjacent elements are the same.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_count = 0\n    current_length = 0\n    \n    for i in range(len(nums)):\n        # If the current element is different from the previous one, \n        # it continues the alternating sequence.\n        if i > 0 and nums[i] != nums[i-1]:\n            current_length += 1\n        else:\n            # If it's the same or the start of the array, reset length to 1.\n            current_length = 1\n        \n        # Every element added to an alternating sequence of length 'current_length'\n        # creates 'current_length' new alternating subarrays ending at index i.\n        total_count += current_length\n        \n    return total_count\n```",
