      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef matrixSum(nums: list[list[int]]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    To find the final score, we sort each row in descending (or ascending) order.\n    The largest number removed from each row in the first step will be the \n    first element of each sorted row. The largest among those becomes the score \n    for that round. We repeat this for each column of the sorted matrix.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Sort every row so that the largest elements are at the same index across rows\n    for row in nums:\n        row.sort()\n    \n    score = 0\n    num_rows = len(nums)\n    num_cols = len(nums[0])\n    \n    # Iterate through each column index\n    for j in range(num_cols):\n        max_in_column = 0\n        # Find the maximum value in the current column across all rows\n        for i in range(num_rows):\n            if nums[i][j] > max_in_column:\n                max_in_column = nums[i][j]\n        # Add the maximum of this \"removal round\" to the score\n        score += max_in_column\n        \n    return score\n```",
