    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minimumSum(nums):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum possible sum of a mountain triplet (i, j, k) such that\n    i < j < k and nums[i] < nums[j] and nums[k] < nums[j].\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(nums)\n    min_sum = float('inf')\n    found = False\n\n    # Since constraints are small (n <= 50), an O(n^3) approach is acceptable.\n    # We iterate through all possible triplets (i, j, k).\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            for k in range(j + 1, n):\n                if nums[i] < nums[j] and nums[k] < nums[j]:\n                    current_sum = nums[i] + nums[j] + nums[k]\n                    if current_sum < min_sum:\n                        min_sum = current_sum\n                        found = True\n                        \n    return min_sum if found else -1\n```",
