    "global index": "LiveCodeBench_45",
    "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. Return the function body without invoking it at the final solution. Question:\nYou are given a 0-indexed integer array nums containing n distinct positive integers. A permutation of nums is called special if:\n\nFor all indexes 0 <= i < n - 1, either nums[i] % nums[i+1] == 0 or nums[i+1] % nums[i] == 0.\n\nReturn the total number of special permutations. As the answer could be large, return it modulo 10^9 + 7.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: nums = [2,3,6]\nOutput: 2\nExplanation: [3,6,2] and [2,6,3] are the two special permutations of nums.\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: nums = [1,4,3]\nOutput: 2\nExplanation: [3,1,4] and [4,1,3] are the two special permutations of nums.\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n2 <= nums.length <= 14\n1 <= nums[i] <= 10^9",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef specialPerm(nums):\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    n = len(nums)\n    # memo[mask][last_idx] stores the number of ways to complete the permutation\n    # starting from the state defined by mask (visited elements) and last_idx (index of the last element added).\n    memo = {}\n\n    def solve(mask, last_idx):\n        # Base case: if all numbers are included in the permutation\n        if mask == (1 << n) - 1:\n            return 1\n        \n        state = (mask, last_idx)\n        if state in memo:\n            return memo[state]\n        \n        count = 0\n        last_val = nums[last_idx]\n        \n        for next_idx in range(n):\n            # Check if the number at next_idx has not been used yet\n            if not (mask & (1 << next_idx)):\n                next_val = nums[next_idx]\n                # Check the divisibility condition\n                if last_val % next_val == 0 or next_val % last_val == 0:\n                    count = (count + solve(mask | (1 << next_idx), next_idx)) % MOD\n        \n        memo[state] = count\n        return count\n\n    total_permutations = 0\n    # Try starting the permutation with every possible number\n    for i in range(n):\n        total_permutations = (total_permutations + solve(1 << i, i)) % MOD\n        \n    return total_permutations\n```",
