      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minimumCost(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    To make all characters equal, we only need to worry about the boundaries where\n    s[i] != s[i+1]. When we encounter such a boundary, we must flip one of the \n    segments (either the prefix up to i or the suffix from i+1) to make them \n    identical. \n    \n    The cost to flip the prefix [0...i] is (i + 1).\n    The cost to flip the suffix [i+1...n-1] is (n - (i + 1)).\n    \n    To minimize the cost, for every index i where s[i] != s[i+1], we choose \n    the minimum of these two costs.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    total_cost = 0\n    \n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        if s[i] != s[i + 1]:\n            # Minimum cost to fix the mismatch between s[i] and s[i+1]\n            total_cost += min(i + 1, n - (i + 1))\n            \n    return total_cost\n```",
