      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read input from stdin\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    n = int(input_data[0])\n    s = input_data[1]\n    \n    t_wins = s.count('T')\n    a_wins = s.count('A')\n    \n    if t_wins > a_wins:\n        print('T')\n    elif a_wins > t_wins:\n        print('A')\n    else:\n        # If wins are tied, find who reached the win count first.\n        # This is equivalent to checking who won the last game among the two,\n        # because the person who reached the tie-score first must be the person\n        # who didn't win the very last game of the match.\n        t_count = 0\n        a_count = 0\n        limit = t_wins # Both reached this number\n        \n        for char in s:\n            if char == 'T':\n                t_count += 1\n            else:\n                a_count += 1\n            \n            if t_count == limit:\n                print('T')\n                break\n            if a_count == limit:\n                print('A')\n                break\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
