      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef find_unique_character_index():\n    # Read the input string from standard input\n    s = sys.stdin.read().strip()\n    \n    # Iterate through the string to compare each character with its neighbors\n    # Length is guaranteed to be at least 3\n    n = len(s)\n    \n    for i in range(n):\n        # Determine the characters to compare against\n        # For the first character, compare with the next two\n        if i == 0:\n            if s[i] != s[i+1] and s[i] != s[i+2]:\n                print(i + 1)\n                return\n        # For the last character, compare with the previous two\n        elif i == n - 1:\n            if s[i] != s[i-1] and s[i] != s[i-2]:\n                print(i + 1)\n                return\n        # For middle characters, it's unique if it differs from neighbors\n        else:\n            if s[i] != s[i-1] and s[i] != s[i+1]:\n                print(i + 1)\n                return\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    find_unique_character_index()\n```",
