      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef findMinimumPartition(nums):\n    \"\"\"\n    To minimize |max(nums1) - min(nums2)|, we should sort the array.\n    Once sorted, for any index i, if we put all elements up to i in nums1 \n    and all elements from i+1 onwards in nums2, then:\n    max(nums1) = nums[i]\n    min(nums2) = nums[i+1]\n    The difference becomes nums[i+1] - nums[i].\n    The minimum such difference across all possible i is our answer.\n    \"\"\"\n    nums.sort()\n    min_diff = float('inf')\n    \n    for i in range(len(nums) - 1):\n        diff = nums[i+1] - nums[i]\n        if diff < min_diff:\n            min_diff = diff\n            \n    return min_diff\n```",
