    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef findMinimumOperations(s1: str, s2: str, s3: str) -> int:\n    # To make strings equal by deleting the rightmost characters,\n    # the resulting strings must be a common prefix of all three.\n    # The longest such prefix determines the minimum operations.\n    \n    # If the first characters are not identical, they can never be made equal\n    # because the operation requires the string length to be at least 2 to delete,\n    # meaning we can never delete the very first character (index 0).\n    if s1[0] != s2[0] or s1[0] != s3[0]:\n        return -1\n    \n    # Find the length of the longest common prefix\n    min_len = min(len(s1), len(s2), len(s3))\n    common_prefix_len = 0\n    \n    for i in range(min_len):\n        if s1[i] == s2[i] == s3[i]:\n            common_prefix_len += 1\n        else:\n            break\n            \n    # Total operations = (chars to remove from s1) + (chars to remove from s2) + (chars to remove from s3)\n    # This simplifies to: (len1 - prefix_len) + (len2 - prefix_len) + (len3 - prefix_len)\n    total_ops = (len(s1) - common_prefix_len) + (len(s2) - common_prefix_len) + (len(s3) - common_prefix_len)\n    \n    return total_ops\n```",
