    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef lengthOfLongestSubsequence(nums, target):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the length of the longest subsequence of nums that sums up to target.\n    This is a variation of the subset sum problem (0/1 Knapsack), \n    where we maximize the number of items instead of their values.\n    \"\"\"\n    # dp[i] will store the maximum length of a subsequence that sums to i.\n    # Initialize with -1 to indicate that the sum is currently unreachable.\n    dp = [-1] * (target + 1)\n    \n    # Base case: a sum of 0 can be achieved with a subsequence of length 0.\n    dp[0] = 0\n    \n    for num in nums:\n        # Iterate backwards to ensure each number is used at most once (0/1 Knapsack logic).\n        # We only go down to 'num' because sums smaller than 'num' cannot be formed using it.\n        for current_sum in range(target, num - 1, -1):\n            # If the previous sum (current_sum - num) was reachable\n            if dp[current_sum - num] != -1:\n                # Update the current sum with the maximum length found so far\n                dp[current_sum] = max(dp[current_sum], dp[current_sum - num] + 1)\n                \n    return dp[target]\n```",
