    "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. Return the function body without invoking it at the final solution. Question:\nYou are given two 0-indexed integer arrays nums1 and nums2, each of length n, and a 1-indexed 2D array queries where queries[i] = [x_i, y_i].\nFor the i^th query, find the maximum value of nums1[j] + nums2[j] among all indices j (0 <= j < n), where nums1[j] >= x_i and nums2[j] >= y_i, or -1 if there is no j satisfying the constraints.\nReturn an array answer where answer[i] is the answer to the i^th query.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: nums1 = [4,3,1,2], nums2 = [2,4,9,5], queries = [[4,1],[1,3],[2,5]]\nOutput: [6,10,7]\nExplanation: \nFor the 1st query x_i = 4 and y_i = 1, we can select index j = 0 since nums1[j] >= 4 and nums2[j] >= 1. The sum nums1[j] + nums2[j] is 6, and we can show that 6 is the maximum we can obtain.\n\nFor the 2nd query x_i = 1 and y_i = 3, we can select index j = 2 since nums1[j] >= 1 and nums2[j] >= 3. The sum nums1[j] + nums2[j] is 10, and we can show that 10 is the maximum we can obtain. \n\nFor the 3rd query x_i = 2 and y_i = 5, we can select index j = 3 since nums1[j] >= 2 and nums2[j] >= 5. The sum nums1[j] + nums2[j] is 7, and we can show that 7 is the maximum we can obtain.\n\nTherefore, we return [6,10,7].\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: nums1 = [3,2,5], nums2 = [2,3,4], queries = [[4,4],[3,2],[1,1]]\nOutput: [9,9,9]\nExplanation: For this example, we can use index j = 2 for all the queries since it satisfies the constraints for each query.\n\nExample 3:\n\nInput: nums1 = [2,1], nums2 = [2,3], queries = [[3,3]]\nOutput: [-1]\nExplanation: There is one query in this example with x_i = 3 and y_i = 3. For every index, j, either nums1[j] < x_i or nums2[j] < y_i. Hence, there is no solution. \n\n \nConstraints:\n\nnums1.length == nums2.length \nn == nums1.length \n1 <= n <= 10^5\n1 <= nums1[i], nums2[i] <= 10^9 \n1 <= queries.length <= 10^5\nqueries[i].length == 2\nx_i == queries[i][1]\ny_i == queries[i][2]\n1 <= x_i, y_i <= 10^9",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef maximumSumQueries(nums1, nums2, queries):\n    import bisect\n\n    n = len(nums1)\n    # Combine nums1 and nums2 and sort by nums1 descending\n    pairs = sorted([(nums1[i], nums2[i]) for i in range(n)], key=lambda x: -x[0])\n    \n    # Sort queries by x_i descending to process them offline\n    # Keep track of original indices to return results in order\n    sorted_queries = sorted([(q[0], q[1], i) for i, q in enumerate(queries)], key=lambda x: -x[0])\n    \n    results = [-1] * len(queries)\n    # Stack will store pairs of (nums2, sum) such that nums2 is strictly increasing\n    # and sum is strictly decreasing. This allows for a monotonic property\n    # to find the maximum sum for a given y_i constraint.\n    stack = []\n    \n    pair_idx = 0\n    for x_i, y_i, original_idx in sorted_queries:\n        # Add all pairs where nums1[j] >= x_i into our candidates structure\n        while pair_idx < n and pairs[pair_idx][0] >= x_i:\n            n1, n2 = pairs[pair_idx]\n            current_sum = n1 + n2\n            \n            # Maintain the monotonic stack:\n            # We want to store pairs (n2, current_sum).\n            # If a new pair has a sum <= an existing pair with a smaller or equal n2, \n            # the new pair is useless.\n            # If a new pair has a sum > an existing pair, and its n2 is >=,\n            # the existing pair might become useless.\n            while stack and stack[-1][1] <= current_sum:\n                stack.pop()\n            \n            if not stack or stack[-1][0] < n2:\n                stack.append((n2, current_sum))\n            \n            pair_idx += 1\n        \n        # Use binary search to find the first pair in stack where stack[j].n2 >= y_i\n        # Since stack is sorted by n2, we find the leftmost element with n2 >= y_i\n        # The first such element will have the maximum sum because sums are decreasing.\n        idx = bisect.bisect_left(stack, (y_i, 0))\n        if idx < len(stack):\n            results[original_idx] = stack[idx][1]\n            \n    return results\n```",
