      "generated_answer": "To find the number of distinct functions mapping a set $A$ (with $m$ elements) into a set $B$ (with $n$ elements), we observe that for each of the $m$ elements in the domain $A$, there are $n$ possible choices in the codomain $B$. Since the choices for each element are independent, the total number of functions is the product of the number of choices for each element: $n \\times n \\times \\dots \\times n$ ($m$ times), which equals $n^m$.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
