      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **F**.\n\nA Support Vector Machine (SVM) finds a $(d-1)$-dimensional hyperplane to separate data in a $d$-dimensional space; therefore, for two-dimensional data ($d=2$), the separating hyperplane is a one-dimensional straight line. Options A, C, G, and H are incorrect as SVMs support multi-class classification, non-linear data (via kernels), and complex hyperplanes. Options B, D, E, I, and J are incorrect because SVM solutions depend on hyperparameters, margins are sensitive to outliers (especially in hard-margin SVMs), and kernels directly influence model complexity.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
