    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To obtain the same projection as Singular Value Decomposition (SVD), the data must be centered because PCA is defined as the SVD of the covariance matrix, which requires the data to have a mean of zero. While SVD can be performed on any matrix, PCA specifically identifies the directions of maximum variance relative to the origin of the data. Therefore, centering the data by subtracting the mean is the necessary step to align the two methods.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
