    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the number of labelled forests on 10 vertices with 5 connected components, such that vertices 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 all belong to different connected components?\n\nOptions: \nA. 70000\nB. 50000\nC. 30000\nD. 55000\nE. 75000\nF. 60000\nG. 45000\nH. 100000\nI. 80000\nJ. 40000\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "This problem can be solved using the generalized version of Cayley's Formula (Cayley's formula for forests). The number of forests on $n$ labeled vertices consisting of $k$ trees such that $k$ specified vertices $v_1, v_2, \\dots, v_k$ belong to different trees is given by the formula $k \\cdot n^{n-k-1}$.\n\nIn this specific case:\n- $n = 10$ (the total number of vertices)\n- $k = 5$ (the number of connected components/trees)\n- Vertices 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 are specified to be in different components.\n\nApplying the formula:\nNumber of forests = $5 \\cdot 10^{10 - 5 - 1}$\nNumber of forests = $5 \\cdot 10^4$\nNumber of forests = $5 \\cdot 10,000 = 50,000$.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
