    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose a convex polygon has 26 faces and 39 edges. How many vertices does it have?\n\nOptions: \nA. 18\nB. 20\nC. 36\nD. 15\nE. 30\nF. 40\nG. 25\nH. 24\nI. 22\nJ. 33\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the number of vertices in a convex polyhedron (the term used for a 3D \"polygon\" with faces), we use Euler's formula: $V - E + F = 2$. Given $F = 26$ and $E = 39$, the equation becomes $V - 39 + 26 = 2$. Solving for $V$ gives $V = 2 + 39 - 26 = 15$.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
