    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the transfer time, we first determine the throughput, which is limited by the bottleneck link (the minimum rate in the path). Assuming $R_3$ is at least 500 kbps (common in such problems where a value might be missing but the bottleneck is $R_1$), the throughput is $R_1 = 500 \\text{ kbps}$. \n\n1. Convert the file size to bits: $4 \\text{ million bytes} \\times 8 \\text{ bits/byte} = 32,000,000 \\text{ bits}$.\n2. Divide the file size by the throughput: $32,000,000 \\text{ bits} / 500,000 \\text{ bits/sec} = 64 \\text{ seconds}$.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
