      "generated_answer": "The channel is defined by $Y = XZ$, where $P(Z=1) = 0.5$ and $P(Z=0) = 0.5$. The transition probabilities are $P(Y=0|X=0)=1$, $P(Y=1|X=0)=0$, $P(Y=0|X=1)=0.5$, and $P(Y=1|X=1)=0.5$. \n\nTo find the capacity $C = \\max_{P(x)} I(X; Y)$, we express the mutual information as $I(X; Y) = H(Y) - H(Y|X)$. Let $P(X=1) = p$; then $P(Y=1) = P(X=1)P(Z=1) = 0.5p$, and $H(Y|X) = P(X=0)H(Y|X=0) + P(X=1)H(Y|X=1) = (1-p) \\cdot 0 + p \\cdot H(0.5) = p$.\n\nMaximizing $I(p) = H(0.5p) - p$ by setting the derivative to zero gives $\\frac{1}{2} \\log_2(\\frac{1-0.5p}{0.5p}) - 1 = 0$, which yields $p = 0.4$. The capacity is $C = H(0.2) - 0.4 \\approx 0.7219 - 0.4 = 0.3219$ bits.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
