      "generated_answer": "For a Markov chain $X \\to Y \\to Z$ of jointly Gaussian variables, the correlation coefficient between $X$ and $Z$ is the product of the correlation coefficients between $X, Y$ and $Y, Z$: $\\rho_{XZ} = \\rho_{XY}\\rho_{YZ} = 0.1 \\times 0.9 = 0.09$. The mutual information for jointly Gaussian variables is given by $I(X;Z) = -\\frac{1}{2} \\log_2(1 - \\rho_{XZ}^2)$. Calculating this gives $I(X;Z) = -\\frac{1}{2} \\log_2(1 - 0.0081) \\approx -\\frac{1}{2} (-0.01174) \\approx 0.00587$ bits.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
