    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the value of the Fourier series coefficient $c_0$, we use the provided formula for $k=0$:\n$$c_0 = \\frac{1}{T} \\int_{-T/2}^{T/2} x(t) e^0 \\, dt = \\frac{1}{10} \\int_{-5}^{5} x(t) \\, dt$$\nCalculating the integral over one period:\n$$\\int_{-5}^{5} x(t) \\, dt = \\int_{-5}^{0} (2) \\, dt + \\int_{0}^{5} (-2) \\, dt = [2t]_{-5}^{0} + [-2t]_{0}^{5} = (0 - (-10)) + (-10 - 0) = 10 - 10 = 0$$\nThus, $c_0 = \\frac{1}{10}(0) = 0$.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
