    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To convert an infix expression to Reverse Polish Notation (RPN), operands remain in their relative order while operators follow their operands according to standard precedence and grouping.\n\n**Expression (a):** `(Z \\downarrow ((((X) \\odot Y) / (X \\odot (Z))) > ((Y) \\equiv X)))`\n1. Inner terms: `(X \\odot Y)` becomes `XY \\odot`, and `(X \\odot Z)` becomes `XZ \\odot`.\n2. Division: `(XY \\odot) / (XZ \\odot)` becomes `XY \\odot XZ \\odot /`.\n3. Equivalence: `(Y \\equiv X)` becomes `YX \\equiv`.\n4. Comparison: `(XY \\odot XZ \\odot /) > (YX \\equiv)` becomes `XY \\odot XZ \\odot / YX \\equiv >`.\n5. Final operator: `Z \\downarrow (...)` becomes `Z XY \\odot XZ \\odot / YX \\equiv > \\downarrow`.\n\n**Expression (b):** `(X / Y) / ((X / X) / (Y / Y))`\n1. Terms: `XY /`, `XX /`, and `YY /`.\n2. Nested division: `(XX /) / (YY /)` becomes `XX / YY / /`.\n3. Final division: `(XY /) / (XX / YY / /)` becomes `XY / XX / YY / / /`.\n\nComparing these results to the options, Option B matches the derived RPN strings exactly.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
