    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A Chord based distributed hash table (DHT) with 26 address space is used in a peer- to-peer file sharing network. There are currently 10 active peers in the network with node ID N1, N11, N15, N23, N31, N40, N45, N51, N60, and N63. Show all the target key (in ascending order, ignore the node's identifier itself) for N1.\n\nOptions: \nA. [11, 15, 23, 31, 40, 45]\nB. [1, 11, 15, 23, 31, 40]\nC. [12, 24, 36, 48, 60, 63]\nD. [3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13]\nE. [2, 3, 5, 9, 17, 33]\nF. [7, 14, 28, 56, 63, 70]\nG. [4, 8, 16, 32, 48, 64]\nH. [13, 26, 39, 52, 65, 78]\nI. [2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12]\nJ. [5, 10, 20, 30, 40, 50]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
