    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The given graph $G$ has edges $E = \\{\\{0,3\\}, \\{1,3\\}, \\{2,3\\}\\}$. This structure is a star graph where node 3 is the central hub connected to all other nodes (0, 1, and 2). A vertex cover is a set of vertices such that every edge in the graph is incident to at least one vertex in the set; since node 3 is incident to all three edges, the set $\\{3\\}$ covers all edges and is the smallest possible set.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
