    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9356",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Consider an additive white Gaussian noise channel with an expected output power constraint $P=2$. Thus $Y = X + Z$, $Z \\sim N(0, 1)$, $Z$ is independent of $X$, and $E(Y)^2 \\leq 2$. Find the channel capacity in bits.\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.25\nB. 2\nC. 4\nD. 0.75\nE. 1\nF. 0.5\nG. 1.75\nH. 3\nI. 2.5\nJ. 1.5\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The channel capacity of an AWGN channel is given by $C = \\frac{1}{2} \\log_2(1 + \\text{SNR})$, where $\\text{SNR} = \\frac{P_X}{N}$. Given the output power constraint $E[Y^2] = E[X^2] + E[Z^2] \\leq 2$ and the noise variance $E[Z^2] = 1$, the maximum input power is $P_X = E[Y^2] - 1 = 2 - 1 = 1$. Substituting these values into the formula yields $C = \\frac{1}{2} \\log_2(1 + \\frac{1}{1}) = \\frac{1}{2} \\log_2(2) = 0.5$ bits.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
