      "generated_answer": "To find the minimum vertex cover, we need to select the smallest set of vertices such that every edge in the graph is incident to at least one vertex in the set.\n\n1.  **Analyze the edges:** The edges are (2,1), (2,0), (2,3), (1,4), and (4,3).\n2.  **Evaluate potential covers:** Vertex 2 covers (2,1), (2,0), and (2,3). The remaining uncovered edges are (1,4) and (4,3), which can both be covered by adding vertex 4.\n3.  **Verify size:** The set [2, 4] covers all edges: (2,1) by 2, (2,0) by 2, (2,3) by 2, (1,4) by 4, and (4,3) by 4. No single vertex covers all edges, and no other pair of vertices from the options covers all five edges (e.g., [2, 3] misses (1,4)).\n\n\\boxed{G}",
