  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9383",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Consider $x(t)$ to be given as, $$ x(t)=10 \\cos (20 \\pi-\\pi / 4)-5 \\cos (50 \\pi t) $$ What is minimum sampling rate (/Hz) such that $y(t)=x(t)$ ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 30\nB. 20\nC. 40\nD. 50\nE. 35\nF. 70\nG. 25\nH. 60\nI. 100\nJ. 80\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the minimum sampling rate (Nyquist rate), we must identify the highest frequency component present in the signal $x(t)$.\n\n1.  The first term $10 \\cos(20\\pi - \\pi/4)$ is a constant (DC component) because it does not depend on the variable $t$; its frequency is $f_1 = 0$ Hz.\n2.  The second term $5 \\cos(50\\pi t)$ has an angular frequency $\\omega_2 = 50\\pi$, which corresponds to a frequency $f_2 = \\frac{50\\pi}{2\\pi} = 25$ Hz.\n3.  The maximum frequency component is $f_{max} = 25$ Hz, and according to the Nyquist-Shannon sampling theorem, the minimum sampling rate required to reconstruct the signal is $f_s = 2 f_{max} = 2 \\times 25 = 50$ Hz.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 186,
        "output_tokens": 217,
