    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the number of questions required in the worst case using an optimal strategy, we use the principles of information theory and binary search. Mary can ask questions that bisect the remaining possibilities (e.g., \"Is the number greater than 500?\"), reducing the search space by half each time. Since $2^9 = 512$ and $2^{10} = 1024$, it takes exactly 10 questions to uniquely identify a specific number among 1,000 possibilities.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
