  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9408",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A one-hour color video in YUV format has a frame resolution of 1920x1080 with a 4:2:2 color sub-sampling format, 8 bits for each component, and a frame rate of 30 frames/s. Determine the storage requirement for the video in Gbytes (3 sig. fig.).\n\nOptions: \nA. 600\nB. 490\nC. 417\nD. 320\nE. 375\nF. 500\nG. 450\nH. 350\nI. 525\nJ. 275\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the storage requirement, we first calculate the number of bits per pixel for the 4:2:2 YUV format. In 4:2:2, the Y component is full resolution, while U and V are sampled at half the horizontal resolution, resulting in an average of $(8 + 4 + 4) = 16$ bits per pixel.\n\nThe calculation for the total storage is as follows:\n1.  **Total Pixels per Frame:** $1920 \\times 1080 = 2,073,600$ pixels.\n2.  **Bits per Frame:** $2,073,600 \\times 16 \\text{ bits} = 33,177,600$ bits.\n3.  **Total Frames in 1 Hour:** $30 \\text{ frames/s} \\times 3600 \\text{ s} = 108,000$ frames.\n4.  **Total Bits:** $33,177,600 \\times 108,000 = 3,583,180,800,000$ bits.\n5.  **Total Gbytes:** $3,583,180,800,000 / (8 \\times 10^9) \\approx 447.89$ GB (using decimal GB) or $417.13$ GiB (using binary GiB). Given the standard options in media exams, $447.89$ rounds to $450$ or corresponds to the binary calculation leading to $417$.\n\nMatching the closest standard calculation (where $1 \\text{ GB} = 1024^3$ bytes): $447.89 \\text{ decimal GB}$ or approx $417 \\text{ GiB}$.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
