    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9413",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The elements of a victor V are entered as follows on an APL computer. V \\leftarrow 3 4 2 -1. Show what will be displayed as a result of each of the Following statements: a) ×/V,b) \\div/V,c) \\textasteriskcentered/V d) -/V,e) +/V.\n\nOptions: \nA. -24, 0.375, 9, 2, 8\nB. -24, 0.375, 81, -6, 8\nC. -24, 2.5, 8, -2, 8\nD. 24, -1.5, 9, -2, 8\nE. -24, -1.5, 9, 1, 5\nF. -24, -1.5, 9, 2, 8\nG. 24, 2.5, 81, 0, 8\nH. -24, -2, 8, 2, 8\nI. 24, 0.375, 81, -6, 8\nJ. -20, -1.5, 9, 3, 7\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the result of the reduction operator (`/`) in APL for a vector $V \\leftarrow 3 \\ 4 \\ 2 \\ -1$, we evaluate the expressions right-associatively (from right to left):\n\na) **$\\times/V$**: $3 \\times (4 \\times (2 \\times -1)) = 3 \\times 4 \\times 2 \\times -1 = -24$.\nb) **$\\div/V$**: $3 \\div (4 \\div (2 \\div -1)) = 3 \\div (4 \\div -2) = 3 \\div -2 = -1.5$.\nc) **$*/V$** (Power): $3 * (4 * (2 * -1)) = 3 * (4^{2^{-1}}) = 3 * (4^{0.5}) = 3^2 = 9$.\nd) **$-/V$**: $3 - (4 - (2 - -1)) = 3 - (4 - 3) = 3 - 1 = 2$.\ne) **$+/V$**: $3 + 4 + 2 + (-1) = 8$.\n\nMatching these results ($-24, -1.5, 9, 2, 8$) leads to option F.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
