    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Determine the period of the following signal, $$ x_1(t)=\\cos (3 \\pi t)-4 \\cos (5 \\pi t-0.5 \\pi) $$\n\nOptions: \nA. 3\nB. 4\nC. 0.5\nD. 3.5\nE. 1.5\nF. 1\nG. 5\nH. 2\nI. 2.5\nJ. 6\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the period of the signal $x_1(t) = \\cos(3\\pi t) - 4\\cos(5\\pi t - 0.5\\pi)$, we first determine the periods of the individual components: $T_1 = \\frac{2\\pi}{3\\pi} = \\frac{2}{3}$ and $T_2 = \\frac{2\\pi}{5\\pi} = \\frac{2}{5}$. The fundamental period $T$ of the sum is the least common multiple (LCM) of $T_1$ and $T_2$, which is calculated as $\\text{LCM}(\\frac{2}{3}, \\frac{2}{5}) = \\frac{\\text{LCM}(2, 2)}{\\text{GCD}(3, 5)} = \\frac{2}{1} = 2$. Therefore, the period of the signal is 2.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
