    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9452",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose a convex 3d-object has k pentagonal faces and m hexagonal faces. All faces are regular. What is k?\n\nOptions: \nA. 16\nB. 5\nC. 10\nD. 12\nE. 15\nF. 8\nG. 14\nH. 25\nI. 18\nJ. 20\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the number of pentagonal faces ($k$), we use Euler's formula for convex polyhedra ($V - E + F = 2$) and the properties of the vertices. Since all faces are regular polygons and the object is convex, it must be a semi-regular (Archimedean) solid or a Platonic solid where exactly three faces meet at each vertex (as four or more hexagons/pentagons would exceed 360 degrees). \n\nIn such a configuration (a \"truncated icosahedron\" or similar structure), every edge is shared by two faces and every vertex is shared by three faces:\n1. $3V = 2E$ (each vertex has degree 3).\n2. $2E = 5k + 6m$ (sum of edges of all faces).\n3. $F = k + m$.\n\nSubstituting these into $V - E + F = 2$:\n$(\\frac{2E}{3}) - E + (k + m) = 2 \\Rightarrow -\\frac{1}{3}E + k + m = 2$\nMultiplying by 6: $-2E + 6k + 6m = 12$\nSubstitute $2E = 5k + 6m$: $-(5k + 6m) + 6k + 6m = 12 \\Rightarrow k = 12$.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
