    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the poles of the digital filter, we first take the Z-transform of the difference equation:\n$Y(z) = \\frac{1}{3}(X(z) + z^{-1}X(z) + z^{-2}X(z))$.\nThe transfer function is $H(z) = \\frac{Y(z)}{X(z)} = \\frac{1}{3}(1 + z^{-1} + z^{-2}) = \\frac{z^2 + z + 1}{3z^2}$.\nThe poles are the roots of the denominator $3z^2 = 0$, which yields a double pole at $z = 0$.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
