    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the capacity of a cascade of $n$ identical Binary Symmetric Channels (BSCs) as $n \\to \\infty$, we analyze the total error probability $P_n$. For a single BSC with error probability $p$, the capacity is $1 - H(p)$. When $n$ channels are cascaded, the total error probability $P_n$ tends toward $1/2$ for any $0 < p < 1$, which represents a completely noisy channel. Since the capacity $C = 1 - H(P_n)$ and $H(1/2) = 1$, the capacity $C$ approaches $1 - 1 = 0$.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
