      "generated_answer": "To find the growth rate of $f(N)$, we observe the recurrence $f(2N) = f(N) + \\log N$. By repeatedly applying the recurrence for $N = 2^k$, we get $f(2^k) = f(2^{k-1}) + \\log(2^{k-1})$, which leads to a summation $f(2^k) = \\sum_{i=0}^{k-1} \\log(2^i) = \\sum_{i=0}^{k-1} i \\log 2$. This sum is proportional to $k^2$, and since $k = \\log_2 N$, the value of $f(N)$ grows as $(\\log N)^2$.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
