      "generated_answer": "The question asks for the total number of bytes written to memory under a **write-through** policy. In a write-through cache, every write operation to the cache is simultaneously (or immediately) written to the main memory.\n\n1.  **Analyze the operations:** The loop executes 256 times. In each iteration `i`, the instruction `A[i] = A[i] + B[2*i]` performs a read of `A[i]`, a read of `B[2*i]`, and exactly one **write** to `A[i]`.\n2.  **Calculate total writes:** There are 256 write operations in total.\n3.  **Calculate total bytes:** Since each element of array A is 4 bytes, the total bytes written to memory is $256 \\text{ elements} \\times 4 \\text{ bytes/element} = 1024 \\text{ bytes}$.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
