    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **G**.\n\n**Explanation:**\nI is true because virtual memory allows the address space to exceed physical RAM by swapping pages to disk. II is false because only the currently needed pages must be in memory (demand paging), and III is false because pages are fixed-size blocks of memory determined by hardware, whereas segments (in segmentation) correspond to semantic units like functions or data structures.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
