      "generated_answer": "The problem $P_1$ (shortest path) can be solved efficiently using algorithms such as Breadth-First Search (BFS) or Dijkstra's algorithm, which run in polynomial time. The problem $P_2$ (longest simple path) is a well-known NP-hard problem, and there is currently no known polynomial-time algorithm to solve it. Therefore, $P_1$ is solvable in polynomial time while $P_2$ is not known to be.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
