      "generated_answer": "A Boolean formula using only the connectives $\\land$ (AND) and $\\lor$ (OR) is **monotone**, meaning that if the formula is true for a given assignment of truth values, it must remain true if any variable is changed from false to true. Condition I is monotone because if at least three variables are true, changing another from false to true still results in at least three being true; however, Conditions II and III are not monotone (e.g., in II, if exactly three are true, changing the fourth to true makes the condition false). Therefore, only Condition I can be represented using only $\\land$ and $\\lor$.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
