      "generated_answer": "Statement 1 is **True** because density estimation can be used to model class-conditional distributions $p(x|C_k)$, which, combined with class priors via Bayes' Theorem, allows for classification (Generative Modeling). Statement 2 is **False** because, while Gaussian Naive Bayes (with shared/identity covariances) implies a logistic functional form, the reverse is not true; logistic regression has fewer parameters and does not assume the data follows a specific Gaussian distribution, meaning the mapping is not a one-to-one correspondence of parameter sets.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
