      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **C**.\n\nStatement 1 is generally considered **True** in the context of statistical learning theory, as SVMs are designed to minimize the structural risk and provide the best generalization guarantees for linear classifiers. Statement 2 is **False** because a generative model with Gaussian distributions (LDA/QDA) results in a linear or quadratic decision boundary; while a quadratic boundary can be represented by a second-degree polynomial kernel, the SVM and the Gaussian model optimize different objective functions (margin maximization vs. density estimation), meaning an SVM might not \"reproduce\" the exact same boundary even if the hypothesis space is sufficient.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
