    "global index": "MMLUPro_philosophy_9607",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Construct a complete truth table for the following argument. Then, using the truth table, determine whether the argument is valid or invalid. If the argument is invalid, choose an option which presents a counterexample. (There may be other counterexamples as well.)\nQ ≡ R\n~(S ∨ Q) / R\n\nOptions: \nA. Invalid. Counterexample when Q, S, and R are false\nB. Invalid. Counterexample when Q is false and S and R are true\nC. Invalid. Counterexample when Q is true, S is false, and R is true\nD. Valid. No counterexample exists\nE. Invalid. Counterexample when Q and S are true and R is false\nF. Invalid. Counterexample when S is true and Q and R are false\nG. Invalid. Counterexample when R is true and Q and S are false\nH. Invalid. Counterexample when Q and R are true and S is false\nI. Valid\nJ. Invalid. Counterexample when Q is true and S and R are false\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
