    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to gate-control theory, which condition tends to close the gate?\n\nOptions: \nA. anxiety\nB. sleep deprivation\nC. focusing on the pain\nD. stress\nE. electrical stimulation\nF. depression\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "According to the gate-control theory of pain, the \"gate\" in the spinal cord can be closed by non-painful sensory input, such as massage or electrical stimulation (e.g., TENS units), which competes with pain signals. Conversely, psychological factors like anxiety, stress, depression, and focusing on the pain tend to open the gate and increase the perception of pain. Therefore, electrical stimulation is the factor among the options that helps close the gate.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
