    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "In a \"split-brain\" patient (where the corpus callosum is severed), sensory information from the left hand is processed in the right hemisphere of the brain. Because the speech centers are located in the left hemisphere for most right-handed individuals, the patient cannot verbally name an object held in the left hand if they cannot see it, as the information cannot cross over to the language centers. Conversely, the right hand remains connected to the left (language) hemisphere, allowing the patient to name objects held in that hand easily.\n\nThe correct letter choice is \\boxed{C}.",
