    "global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1883",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the degree ofskewnessof the distribution representing thesedata. Class Limit Frequency Class Midpoint 49 - 54 6 51.5 55 - 60 15 57.5 61 - 66 24 63.5 67 - 72 33 69.5 73 - 78 22 75.5\n\nOptions: \nA. 2.1\nB. - .89\nC. 0.58\nD. - .44\nE. 0.33\nF. 1.67\nG. 1.2\nH. 0.99\nI. -0.75\nJ. -1.05\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the degree of skewness (typically Pearson's Coefficient of Skewness), we first calculate the mean, median, and standard deviation of the frequency distribution. \n\n1.  **Calculate the Mean ($\\bar{x}$):** $\\sum(f \\cdot x) / \\sum f = (309 + 862.5 + 1524 + 2293.5 + 1661) / 100 = 6650 / 100 = 66.5$.\n2.  **Calculate the Median:** With $N=100$, the median is at the 50th value, which falls in the 67-72 class; using the formula $L + [\\frac{N/2 - CF_{prev}}{f}] \\cdot w = 66.5 + [\\frac{50 - 45}{33}] \\cdot 6 \\approx 67.41$.\n3.  **Calculate the Standard Deviation ($s$):** $\\sqrt{\\frac{\\sum f(x - \\bar{x})^2}{N}} \\approx 7.02$; then calculate skewness using $3(\\bar{x} - \\text{median}) / s \\approx 3(66.5 - 67.41) / 7.02 \\approx -0.39$.\n\nComparing the calculated value to the options, -0.44 is the closest statistical representation provided.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
