    "global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_1849",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A college freshman obtains a score of 150 on his English final exam, a score of 100 on his math exam, a score of 55 on his chemistry exam, and a score of 30 on his history exam. The means and standard deviations for these tests are, respectively, 125 and 20 for the English exam, 90 and 10 for the math exam, 45 and 5 for the chemistry exam, and 30 and 5 for the history exam. Based on this information, you can conclude that the young man's test performance was best on which exam?\n\nOptions: \nA. Math and History\nB. math\nC. Chemistry and History\nD. English and Math\nE. All of the above\nF. history\nG. English\nH. chemistry\nI. English and History\nJ. None of the above\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine on which exam the student performed best, we calculate the z-score (standard score) for each subject using the formula $z = \\frac{x - \\mu}{\\sigma}$.\n\n*   **English:** $z = \\frac{150 - 125}{20} = 1.25$\n*   **Math:** $z = \\frac{100 - 90}{10} = 1.0$\n*   **Chemistry:** $z = \\frac{55 - 45}{5} = 2.0$\n*   **History:** $z = \\frac{30 - 30}{5} = 0$\n\nComparing the z-scores, the student performed best in Chemistry because it has the highest relative standing (2.0 standard deviations above the mean).\n\n\\boxed{H}",
