    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "In most jurisdictions, employment laws prohibit discrimination based on age. However, an employer may legally ask for an applicant's age if it is a **bona fide occupational requirement (BFOQ)**, meaning the age requirement is reasonably necessary to the normal operation of that particular business (e.g., legal age to serve alcohol or age requirements for child actors). Other options, such as curiosity or company policy, do not override legal protections against age discrimination.\n\nThe correct letter choice is \\boxed{B}.",
