    "global index": "MMLU_formal_logic_99",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Construct a complete truth table for the following pairs of propositions. Then, using the truth tables, determine whether the statements are logically equivalent or contradictory. If neither, determine whether they are consistent or inconsistent. Justify your answers.\n(G ∨ ~H) ⊃ G and ~G ≡ (~H · G)\n\nOptions: \nA. Logically equivalent\nB. Contradictory\nC. Neither logically equivalent nor contradictory, but consistent\nD. Inconsistent\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the relationship between the two propositions, we construct a truth table for $(G \\lor \\neg H) \\supset G$ and $\\neg G \\equiv (\\neg H \\cdot G)$:\n\n| $G$ | $H$ | $\\neg G$ | $\\neg H$ | $G \\lor \\neg H$ | $(G \\lor \\neg H) \\supset G$ | $\\neg H \\cdot G$ | $\\neg G \\equiv (\\neg H \\cdot G)$ |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| T | T | F | F | T | **T** | F | **T** |\n| T | F | F | T | T | **T** | T | **F** |\n| F | T | F | F | F | **T** | F | **T** |\n| F | F | T | T | T | **F** | F | **F** |\n\nComparing the columns for the two propositions (T, T, T, F vs. T, F, T, F), we see they are not identical (not equivalent) and never both false at the same time in a way that suggests contradiction; however, they are **consistent** because there are rows (the 1st and 3rd) where both statements are true simultaneously. Since they are neither equivalent nor contradictory but share at least one true valuation, they are consistent.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
