    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the most economical option, we calculate the area of carpet required for each width based on the room dimensions (14.5' x 11.25'):\n1.  **12' Width:** You would buy a 12' wide piece by 14'6\" (14.5') long. Area = $12 \\times 14.5 = 174 \\text{ sq. ft.} = 19.33 \\text{ sq. yd.}$ Cost = $19.33 \\times \\$11.95 \\approx \\$231.03$.\n2.  **15' Width:** You would buy a 15' wide piece by 11'3\" (11.25') long. Area = $15 \\times 11.25 = 168.75 \\text{ sq. ft.} = 18.75 \\text{ sq. yd.}$ Cost = $18.75 \\times \\$11.95 = \\$224.0625$.\n\nThe 15' width is more economical at a cost of $224.06.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
