  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_247",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose we are given the following information. Use this information to calculate abnormal return. Rf: 4%\nRm: 12%\nBeta of the Portfolio: 1.8\nBeginning Value of Portfolio: $50,000\nEnding Value of Portfolio: $60,000\nWhat is the abnormal return?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.025\nB. 0.035\nC. 0.016\nD. 0.012\nE. 0.030\nF. 0.040\nG. 0.008\nH. 0.010\nI. 0.020\nJ. 0.050\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the abnormal return (Alpha), we first calculate the actual return and the expected return based on the Capital Asset Pricing Model (CAPM).\n\n1.  **Actual Return ($R_p$):** $\\frac{\\text{Ending Value} - \\text{Beginning Value}}{\\text{Beginning Value}} = \\frac{60,000 - 50,000}{50,000} = 0.20$ (or 20%).\n2.  **Expected Return ($E[R_p]$):** $R_f + \\beta(R_m - R_f) = 0.04 + 1.8(0.12 - 0.04) = 0.04 + 1.8(0.08) = 0.04 + 0.144 = 0.184$ (or 18.4%).\n3.  **Abnormal Return:** $R_p - E[R_p] = 0.20 - 0.184 = 0.016$.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
