    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the certainty equivalent (CE), we first calculate the expected utility of the total salary $X$, where $X = \\{80000, 90000, 100000, 110000, 120000, 130000, 140000\\}$ with equal probability $p = 1/7$.\nThe expected utility is $E[U(X)] = \\frac{1}{7} \\sum x_i^{1/4} \\approx \\frac{16.8179 + 17.3205 + 17.7828 + 18.2116 + 18.6121 + 18.9883 + 19.3434}{7} \\approx 18.1538$.\nSetting $U(CE) = CE^{1/4} = 18.1538$ and solving for $CE$ gives $CE = (18.1538)^4 \\approx 108,610$.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
