      "generated_answer": "To find the number of tiles, first convert the floor dimensions from feet to inches: 9 feet is 108 inches and 6 feet is 72 inches. The number of tiles needed is $(108 \\div 9) \\times (72 \\div 9) = 12 \\times 8 = 96$ tiles. At 75 cents each, the total cost is $96 \\times 0.75 = 72$ dollars.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
