    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "In the Bertrand model of competition, firms compete on price. Since the products are identical and there are no costs of production (marginal cost $MC = 0$), firms will continue to undercut each other's prices to capture the entire market until the price equals marginal cost. Therefore, in the Nash equilibrium, $P_1 = P_2 = MC = 0$.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
