    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_560",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let $P(r,t,T)$ denote the price at time $t$ of $1 to be paid with certainty at time $T, t\\leT$, if the short rate at time $t$ is equal to $r$. For a Vasicek model you are given: $P(0.04, 0, 2)=0.9445$, $P(0.05, 1, 3)=0.9321$, $P(r^*, 2, 4)=0.8960$. What is $r^*$?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.11\nB. 0.06\nC. 0.05\nD. 0.04\nE. 0.08\nF. 0.12\nG. 0.07\nH. 0.09\nI. 0.10\nJ. 0.03\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "In the Vasicek model, the bond price is given by $P(r, t, T) = A(t, T) e^{-B(t, T)r}$. Since the time to maturity $(T-t) = 2$ is constant for all three given scenarios, let $A = A(2)$ and $B = B(2)$.\n\nWe have two equations to solve for the constants $A$ and $B$:\n1. $0.9445 = A e^{-0.04B}$\n2. $0.9321 = A e^{-0.05B}$\n\nDividing the two equations: $\\frac{0.9445}{0.9321} = \\frac{e^{-0.04B}}{e^{-0.05B}} = e^{0.01B}$. Taking the natural log: $\\ln(1.0133) \\approx 0.0132 = 0.01B$, so $B \\approx 1.32$.\nUsing the third price: $0.8960 = A e^{-r^* B}$. Dividing the first equation by this gives: $\\frac{0.9445}{0.8960} = e^{B(r^* - 0.04)}$.\n$1.05413 = e^{1.32(r^* - 0.04)} \\implies \\ln(1.05413) \\approx 0.0527 = 1.32(r^* - 0.04) \\implies r^* - 0.04 = 0.0399 \\approx 0.04$. Thus, $r^* \\approx 0.08$.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 271,
        "output_tokens": 399,
        "total_tokens": 670
      },
      "provider": "google",
      "error": null,
