    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Assessments of leadership styles are often subjective and depend on the specific criteria used by political scientists; however, \"transformational\" leaders are typically defined as those who fundamentally shift a nation's systems, values, or global standing. In this context, Bill Clinton is often categorized as a \"transactional\" leader because his presidency focused more on incremental policy adjustments, pragmatism, and maintaining stability during a period of prosperity rather than systemic upheaval. Consequently, within academic frameworks comparing these specific figures, he is the least likely to be labeled transformational.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
