  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_196",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is not an advantage of a hierarchical structure?\n\nOptions: \nA. Clear responsibilities and roles\nB. Discipline and stability\nC. Quick response to change\nD. Clear chain of command\nE. Promotion opportunities\nF. High flexibility\nG. Easy to manage\nH. Small span of control\nI. Enhanced communication\nJ. Improved employee motivation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is **C** (or **F**, as both relate to flexibility), but in most business management contexts, **C** is the standard answer for what a hierarchical structure lacks.\n\nHierarchical structures are characterized by multiple layers of management and rigid chains of command, which makes them slow to adapt to market changes. Unlike flat structures, the bureaucratic nature of a hierarchy often hinders quick decision-making and fluid internal communication. Therefore, a \"quick response to change\" is considered a disadvantage or a missing feature rather than an advantage.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
