      "generated_answer": "Stagflation occurs when an economy experiences stagnant economic growth, high unemployment, and high inflation simultaneously. This phenomenon is typically caused by a \"supply shock,\" which is represented graphically as a decrease (leftward shift) in the short-run aggregate supply curve. This shift leads to both an increase in the price level (inflation) and a decrease in real GDP (higher unemployment).\n\n\\boxed{F}",
