    "global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5584",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Crowding out\n\nOptions: \nA. occurs when interest rates fall due to government borrowing.\nB. occurs when consumers and firms spend less offsetting expansionary fiscal policy.\nC. occurs when the government reduces its spending in response to inflation.\nD. is a consequence of contractionary fiscal policy.\nE. is one reason fiscal policy is so effective.\nF. is when expansionary fiscal policy leads to a decrease in interest rates.\nG. happens when the government increases taxes to reduce the budget deficit.\nH. causes the aggregate demand curve to shift to the right.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
