      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **B**.\n\nCrowding out refers to the reduction in private consumption or investment that occurs when expansionary fiscal policy (such as increased government spending) leads to higher interest rates or higher taxes, thereby offsetting the initial boost to aggregate demand. While it typically involves rising interest rates (making options A and F incorrect), option B most accurately describes the resulting behavior of firms and consumers that diminishes the policy's effectiveness.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
