    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the difference between \"caveat emptor\" and \"ceteris paribus\"\n\nOptions: \nA. 'Caveat emptor' is 'Buyer's guarantee' and 'Ceteris paribus' is 'given the circumstances'\nB. 'Caveat emptor' is 'Buyer beware' and 'Ceteris paribus' is 'all things constant'\nC. 'Caveat emptor' is 'Let the buyer beware' and 'Ceteris paribus' is 'all other things being equal'\nD. 'Caveat emptor' is 'Let the buyer choose' and 'Ceteris paribus' is 'other things unchanged'\nE. 'Caveat emptor' is 'Let the seller beware' and 'Ceteris paribus' is 'all things considered'\nF. 'Caveat emptor' means 'Seller's warning' and 'Ceteris paribus' means 'everything else is variable'\nG. 'Caveat emptor' is 'The seller is responsible' and 'Ceteris paribus' is 'all factors constant'\nH. 'Caveat emptor' is 'buyer's choice' and 'Ceteris paribus' is 'equal rights'\nI. 'Caveat emptor' means 'Guarantee for the buyer' and 'Ceteris paribus' means 'considering each part'\nJ. 'Caveat emptor' is 'Let the buyer decide' and 'Ceteris paribus' is 'with all other things'\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
