      "generated_answer": "A negative supply shock (such as a sudden increase in energy prices) increases both inflation and unemployment simultaneously, a phenomenon known as stagflation. Because the Phillips curve represents the trade-off between inflation and unemployment, an increase in both variables at every level requires the curve to shift outward or to the right. Therefore, a contractionary supply shock shifts the short-run Phillips curve to the right.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
      "success": true,
