    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "According to the balance of payments accounting identity, the sum of the current account, the capital account, and the financial account must equal zero ($CA + KA + FA = 0$). If a country has a negative current account (a deficit), it must be offset by a surplus of equal magnitude in the capital and financial accounts combined. Among the provided choices, the most direct accounting necessity is that the value must be balanced by the other accounts.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
