    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "In economics, a **positive statement** is an objective claim about how the world works that can be tested or verified with data, whereas a normative statement expresses a value judgment (often using words like \"should\" or \"ought\"). Option J is a positive statement because it describes a verifiable relationship between the law of increasing costs and the technical shape of the production possibilities frontier. Options B, G, H, I, and E are normative, while A, C, and D are factually incorrect economic assertions.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
