    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following statements is TRUE concerning the standard regression model?\n\nOptions: \nA. y has a probability distribution\nB. x has a probability distribution\nC. The disturbance term is assumed to be correlated with x\nD. For an adequate model, the residual (u-hat) will be zero for all sample data points\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "In the standard (classical) linear regression model, $y$ is a random variable because it is a function of the stochastic disturbance term, whereas $x$ is typically assumed to be fixed (non-stochastic) in repeated sampling. Option C is incorrect because the disturbance term must be uncorrelated with $x$ (exogeneity), and Option D is incorrect because residuals are almost never zero in the presence of random error. Thus, $y$ follows a probability distribution determined by the error term.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
