    "global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5993",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The characteristic roots of the MA process\n\n$y_t = -3u_{{t-1}} + u_{{t-2}} + u_t$\n\nare\n\nOptions: \nA. 1 and 0.5\nB. 2 and 0.5\nC. -1 and -0.5\nD. -1 and 2\nE. 3 and -2\nF. 1 and 2\nG. 1 and -3\nH. -3 and -0.5\nI. 1 and -2\nJ. 2 and -0.5\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the characteristic roots of the Moving Average (MA) process $y_t = u_t - 3u_{t-1} + u_{t-2}$, we express it using the backshift operator $L$: $y_t = (1 - 3L + L^2)u_t$. The characteristic equation is derived from the operator polynomial $1 - 3z + z^2 = 0$. Using the quadratic formula $z = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}$, we get $z = \\frac{3 \\pm \\sqrt{9 - 4}}{2}$, which results in $z_1 = \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{5}}{2} \\approx 2.618$ and $z_2 = \\frac{3 - \\sqrt{5}}{2} \\approx 0.382$; however, looking at the provided integer/simple fraction options, the question likely refers to the roots of a process where the coefficients are factored differently or contains a typo, but the standard solution for coefficients $1, -3, 1$ does not match the options. Re-evaluating the polynomial as $z^2 - 3z + 2 = 0$ (which matches option F) suggests a common textbook variation where the roots are $1$ and $2$.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
