    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: To close an expansionary gap\n\nOptions: \nA. the aggregate demand curve should not be shifted.\nB. the aggregate demand curve should be shifted to the right.\nC. the aggregate supply curve should be shifted to the left.\nD. both the aggregate demand and supply curves should not be shifted.\nE. the aggregate supply curve should be shifted to the right, and the aggregate demand curve to the left.\nF. the aggregate supply curve should be shifted to the right.\nG. the aggregate demand curve should be shifted to the left.\nH. both the aggregate demand and supply curves should be shifted to the left.\nI. the aggregate supply curve should not be shifted.\nJ. both the aggregate demand and supply curves should be shifted to the right.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "An expansionary (or inflationary) gap occurs when the current equilibrium level of real GDP exceeds potential GDP, often leading to inflation. To close this gap using fiscal or monetary policy, the goal is to decrease total spending in the economy, which is represented by shifting the aggregate demand curve to the left. This reduction in demand brings the economy back toward its potential output level.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
