      "generated_answer": "To address residual non-normality, one must often address the underlying distribution of the error terms or the functional form of the model.\n\n**A. Use a logarithmic functional form instead of a linear one** is the most plausible response because taking logs often \"compresses\" the scale of the data, reducing skewness and helping the residuals follow a normal distribution. While removing outliers (Option D) is a common practice, it is generally discouraged as a first step unless the data points are proven errors, whereas changing the functional form addresses the model's structural fit.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
