    "global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6115",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose that a hypothesis test is conducted using a 5% significance level. Which of the following statements are correct?\n\n(i) The significance level is equal to the size of the test\n\n(ii) The significance level is equal to the power of the test\n\n(iii) 2.5% of the total distribution will be in each tail rejection region for a 2-sided test\n\n(iv) 5% of the total distribution will be in each tail rejection region for a 2-sided test.\n\nOptions: \nA. (ii), (iii), and (iv) only\nB. (i), (ii), and (iii) only\nC. (ii) and (iii) only\nD. (i), (iii), and (iv) only\nE. (iii) and (iv) only\nF. (ii) and (iv) only\nG. (i) and (iv) only\nH. (i) and (iii) only\nI. (i) and (ii) only\nJ. (i), (ii), (iii), and (iv)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is determined by evaluating each statement: (i) is true because the significance level ($\\alpha$) is by definition the size of the test; (ii) is false because power is $1 - \\beta$ (where $\\beta$ is Type II error), not $\\alpha$; (iii) is true because a two-sided test splits the significance level equally between the two tails ($5\\% / 2 = 2.5\\%$ per tail); and (iv) is false as it describes a $10\\%$ significance level. Therefore, only statements (i) and (iii) are correct.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
