      "generated_answer": "The \"Lotus principle\" originates from the 1927 Permanent Court of International Justice (PCIJ) case involving a collision between the French steamer *Lotus* and the Turkish steamer *Boz-Kourt*. It establishes that sovereign states may act in any way they wish so long as they do not contravene an explicit prohibition in international law. This is often summarized as \"whatever is not prohibited is permitted.\"\n\n\\boxed{G}",
