    "global index": "MMLUPro_law_1671",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Generally, erotic materials are protected by the First Amendment for a person's personal use and possession. However, certain erotic material can reach a point where it steps over the boundaries of First Amendment protection. The Supreme Court has held that if material is obscene it does not mandate First Amendment protection. Which of the following most accurately represents one of the prongs of the three-pronged test enunciated by the U.S. Supreme Court's for determining whether a film, book, video or pictorial is obscene and therefore not subject to protection?\n\nOptions: \nA. Whether the work, taken as a whole, is considered to be offensive or inappropriate by the majority of the population.\nB. Whether the work, taken as a whole and judged by contemporary community standards, would be seen by a sensitive or vulnerable person to appeal to the prurient interest.\nC. Whether the work, taken as a whole, has been classified as obscene by a government authority.\nD. Whether the work, when examined from an individual perspective, incites violent or harmful actions.\nE. Whether the work has been properly judged from a national standard to offend sensitive standards of community morals.\nF. Whether the work, taken as a whole, lacks serious literary, artistic, political, or scientific value.\nG. Whether the work, in its entirety, promotes or glorifies illegal activities.\nH. Whether the work, when viewed in its entirety, defames or slanders any person or group.\nI. Whether the work, judged from a global perspective, offends common decency or morality.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
