      "generated_answer": "The Supreme Court established the \"Miller test\" in *Miller v. California* (1973) to determine whether material is obscene. The three prongs include: (1) whether the average person, applying contemporary community standards, would find that the work appeals to the prurient interest; (2) whether the work depicts sexual conduct in a patently offensive way; and (3) whether the work, taken as a whole, lacks serious literary, artistic, political, or scientific value. Option F directly identifies the third prong of this legal test.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
