      "generated_answer": "The enactment will most likely be declared unconstitutional because providing direct state subsidies for the salaries of teachers in private religious schools creates an \"excessive entanglement\" between government and religion. Under the *Lemon* test (and specifically cases like *Lemon v. Kurtzman*), such direct aid is prohibited because the state cannot easily ensure that teachers in a religious environment are not performing religious functions without constant, intrusive monitoring. Because this is a state statute being applied to the First Amendment, it involves the Amendment's application to the states via the Fourteenth Amendment.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
