      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **H**.\n\nThe company’s discriminatory policy constitutes \"state action\" because the county is significantly involved: it owns and developed the land, receives a percentage of profits as rent, and specifically approved the bylaws. Under the Equal Protection Clause, gender-based classifications are subject to \"intermediate scrutiny,\" meaning the plaintiff will prevail unless the company (as a state actor) can show the exclusion of women serves an important governmental objective and is substantially related to that objective.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
