      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **A**.\n\nThe Commerce Clause provides the strongest constitutional basis because the news media is an instrumental part of interstate commerce, giving Congress broad authority to regulate its activities. While Option B (Supremacy Clause) explains what happens when laws conflict, it does not provide an independent source of power for Congress to enact the law in the first place. Option C is less certain because the Supreme Court has previously held (in *Branzburg v. Hayes*) that the First Amendment does not inherently grant journalists a testimonial privilege.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
