    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is based on the **Exceptions Clause** found in Article III, Section 2 of the U.S. Constitution. This clause grants Congress the explicit power to make \"exceptions\" and \"regulations\" regarding the Supreme Court's appellate jurisdiction, a principle upheld in cases such as *Ex parte McCardle*. While there are modern constitutional limits to this power, it remains the most direct and persuasive textual argument for such a statute.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
