    "global index": "QANTA_Social Science_907",
    "prompt": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Herfindahl Index calculates how well this condition is being met in an industry.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The Herfindahl Index (also known as the Herfindahl-Hirschman Index or HHI) is a common measure of market concentration used to determine the level of competition within an industry. It is calculated by squaring the market share of each firm in the market and summing the resulting figures. Regulatory bodies use this index to assess whether a market is competitive or approaching a monopoly.\n\n\\boxed{Competition}",
