    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let $A$ be the initial number of adults and $T$ be the initial total number of people. From the first condition, $\\frac{A}{T} = \\frac{5}{12}$, which implies $A = 5k$ and $T = 12k$ for some positive integer $k$.\n\nLet $x$ be the number of adults among the 50 new people ($0 \\le x \\le 50$). After the bus arrives, the new ratio of adults is $\\frac{A+x}{T+50} = \\frac{11}{25}$, which leads to the equation:\n$25(5k + x) = 11(12k + 50) \\implies 125k + 25x = 132k + 550 \\implies 25x - 550 = 7k$.\nFor $k$ to be an integer, $25x - 550$ must be a multiple of 7. Testing values for $x$ starting from $x=23$ (since $25x > 550$):\nIf $x = 23$, $25(23) - 550 = 575 - 550 = 25$ (not div. by 7).\nIf $x = 24$, $25(24) - 550 = 50$ (not div. by 7).\nIf $x = 29$, $25(29) - 550 = 725 - 550 = 175$, which gives $k = \\frac{175}{7} = 25$.\n\nWith $k=25$ and $x=29$, the number of adults after the bus arrives is $A+x = 5(25) + 29 = 125 + 29 = 154$. Since $k$ must be a positive integer and $x \\le 50$, this is the smallest valid configuration.\n\n\\boxed{154}",
