    "global index": "AIME_75",
    "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Among the 900 residents of Aimeville, there are 195 who own a diamond ring, 367 who own a set of golf clubs, and 562 who own a garden spade. In addition, each of the 900 residents owns a bag of candy hearts. There are 437 residents who own exactly two of these things, and 234 residents who own exactly three of these things. Find the number of residents of Aimeville who own all four of these things.\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To solve this problem, we define the four sets of items: $D$ (diamond ring), $G$ (golf clubs), $S$ (garden spade), and $C$ (candy hearts). We are given that everyone owns a bag of candy hearts, so $C$ contains all 900 residents.\n\nLet $n_i$ be the number of residents who own exactly $i$ items. We know $n_1 + n_2 + n_3 + n_4 = 900$. We are given $n_2 = 437$ and $n_3 = 234$. From the first equation, we find $n_1 + n_4 = 900 - 437 - 234 = 229$.\n\nThe sum of the sizes of the sets counts each person $i$ times, where $i$ is the number of items they own. Thus, $|D| + |G| + |S| + |C| = 1 \\cdot n_1 + 2 \\cdot n_2 + 3 \\cdot n_3 + 4 \\cdot n_4$. Substituting the given values:\n$195 + 367 + 562 + 900 = n_1 + 2(437) + 3(234) + 4n_4$\n$2024 = n_1 + 874 + 702 + 4n_4$\n$2024 = n_1 + 1576 + 4n_4 \\implies n_1 + 4n_4 = 448$\n\nWe now have a system of two equations:\n1) $n_1 + n_4 = 229$\n2) $n_1 + 4n_4 = 448$\nSubtracting the first equation from the second gives $3n_4 = 219$, which results in $n_4 = 73$.\n\n\\boxed{73}",
