      "generated_answer": "To solve this problem, let $x$ be the fare for the first kilometer and $y$ be the rate per kilometer for the remaining distance. We can set up two linear equations based on the given information:\n1) $x + (20 - 1)y = 37.70 \\Rightarrow x + 19y = 37.70$\n2) $x + (26 - 1)y = 48.50 \\Rightarrow x + 25y = 48.50$\n\nSubtracting the first equation from the second gives $6y = 10.80$, which simplifies to $y = 1.80$. Substituting $y = 1.80$ back into the first equation, we get $x + 19(1.80) = 37.70 \\Rightarrow x + 34.20 = 37.70$, which simplifies to $x = 3.50$.\n\nThe fare for the first kilometer is $3.50 and the fare for each successive kilometer is $1.80.\n\n\\boxed{First\\ km: \\$3.50, Successive\\ km: \\$1.80}",
