      "generated_answer": "In an isosceles triangle, there are two possible cases based on whether the given 54° angle is the vertex angle or a base angle.\n\n1.  **Case 1: The 54° angle is the vertex angle.** The sum of the base angles is $180^\\circ - 54^\\circ = 126^\\circ$, so each base angle is $126^\\circ / 2 = 63^\\circ$.\n2.  **Case 2: The 54° angle is a base angle.** By definition, the two base angles of an isosceles triangle are equal, so the other base angle must also be $54^\\circ$.\n\nThus, the possible values for the base angles are 63° or 54°.\n\n\\boxed{63^\\circ \\text{ or } 54^\\circ}",
