    "global index": "AsDiv_1428",
    "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Points A and B are 70 km apart on a highway. A car starts from A and another car starts from B at the same time. If they travel in the same direction, they meet in 7 hours, but if they travel towards each other they meet in one hour.\n\nQuestion: What are their respective speeds?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "gemini-3-flash-preview",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the speeds of the two cars, let the speed of the car starting from A be $x$ km/h and the speed of the car starting from B be $y$ km/h.\n\n1.  When traveling in the same direction, the relative speed is the difference of their speeds ($x - y$), and since they meet in 7 hours over a distance of 70 km, we have $7(x - y) = 70$, which simplifies to $x - y = 10$.\n2.  When traveling towards each other, the relative speed is the sum of their speeds ($x + y$), and since they meet in 1 hour, we have $1(x + y) = 70$, which simplifies to $x + y = 70$.\n3.  Solving this system of linear equations ($x - y = 10$ and $x + y = 70$) by adding them gives $2x = 80$, so $x = 40$; substituting $x$ back into the second equation gives $40 + y = 70$, so $y = 30$.\n\nThe speeds of the two cars are 40 km/h and 30 km/h.\n\n\\boxed{40 \\text{ km/h and } 30 \\text{ km/h}}",
