    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the basic first class full fare ($F$) and the reservation charge ($R$), we can set up a system of linear equations based on the given information.\n\n1.  From the cost of one reserved full ticket: $F + R = 216$\n2.  From the cost of one full and one half reserved ticket: $(F + R) + (\\frac{1}{2}F + R) = 327$\n\nSubstituting the first equation into the second, we get $216 + \\frac{1}{2}F + R = 327$, which simplifies to $\\frac{1}{2}F + R = 111$. Subtracting this new equation from the first ($F + R = 216$), we find $\\frac{1}{2}F = 105$, which gives $F = 210$; substituting $F$ back into the first equation gives $210 + R = 216$, so $R = 6$.\n\nBasic first class full fare: $210, Reservation charge: $6.\n\n\\boxed{F = 210, R = 6}",
