    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "In the Demographic Transition Model, Stage 3 is characterized by a significant decline in the birth rate due to social changes and the widespread diffusion of fertility control (contraception). While the transition begins at the end of Stage 2, it is during Stage 3 that these practices become a defining characteristic of the demographic shift. Consequently, the birth rate begins to